{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/shim.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730119Z","id":"6c8263c15b4e53e447a913833b9f54feebc1208cb582a2b082a0d920ca3608ac","body":{"detail":"Not taken (2026-10-01, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-01-grok-build.md:115 (Q2)): sandboxed Grok is unsupported unless a daemon already runs; under the workspace, read-only and strict profiles a daemon the shim starts cannot write ~/.clax (docs/contract.md:4203-4207). Supporting it needs sandbox detection in the shim and a daemon start outside the sandbox; the contract's Known-limitations entry then goes.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":185},"end":{"line":193},"content_hash":"640b44f0e9381845d6a718e1018b787e83435bdbaa898535326273c8c39a837e"},"summary":"Support Grok's sandbox: detect it in the shim and start the daemon outside it","tags":["revisit:Grok users run with the sandbox on and no daemon started outside it","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/shim.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:29:45.207442Z","id":"038844cbfbf4e93c7ee1ab9b9872d06464c08dc181ebba1142ea5010aff757c3","body":{"detail":"Not taken (2026-10-01, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-01-grok-build.md:115 (Q2)): sandboxed Grok is unsupported unless a daemon already runs; under the workspace, read-only and strict profiles a daemon the shim starts cannot write ~/.clax (docs/contract.md:4203-4207). Supporting it needs sandbox detection in the shim and a daemon start outside the sandbox; the contract's Known-limitations entry then goes.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":190},"end":{"line":198},"content_hash":"d9959f5d584066d4e69e140993450c2f50d43d874d097d9bac813fe993476b6a"},"summary":"Support Grok's sandbox: detect it in the shim and start the daemon outside it","supersedes":"6c8263c15b4e53e447a913833b9f54feebc1208cb582a2b082a0d920ca3608ac","tags":["revisit:Grok users run with the sandbox on and no daemon started outside it","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/shim.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.619083Z","id":"7b5749bd659189973546d590ce7735c100bcab247f10b10d99fc6fae4018ce9e","body":{"detail":"Not taken (2026-10-01, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-01-grok-build.md:115 (Q2)): sandboxed Grok is unsupported unless a daemon already runs; under the workspace, read-only and strict profiles a daemon the shim starts cannot write ~/.clax (docs/contract.md:4203-4207). Supporting it needs sandbox detection in the shim and a daemon start outside the sandbox; the contract's Known-limitations entry then goes.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":198},"end":{"line":206},"content_hash":"d9959f5d584066d4e69e140993450c2f50d43d874d097d9bac813fe993476b6a"},"summary":"Support Grok's sandbox: detect it in the shim and start the daemon outside it","supersedes":"038844cbfbf4e93c7ee1ab9b9872d06464c08dc181ebba1142ea5010aff757c3","tags":["revisit:Grok users run with the sandbox on and no daemon started outside it","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.889533Z","id":"8bd3a5dd80c39c3894d638d0d133c7b5d69653c3624ef606ea9bccdf08f95e67","body":{"detail":"A withheld anchor's file is null in the thread view (crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs placeholder::anchor, spec §8.3), and comments_read maps a null file to INDEX_FILE here, so the agent is told the thread is on index.html. No withheld text leaks; the file it names may be wrong. The shim's view of withheld fields (anchor_withheld, clip_withheld, withheld) is not formatted yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":567},"end":{"line":567},"content_hash":"1c7991c30f6eeaff531e82713cb230c0447e5b7f4ea8affd5c54ab6e58c9b6d7"},"suggested_fix":"When the thread is anchor_withheld, give file null (or say the anchor is withheld) and carry the withheld summary into the tool result, with the rest of the tiers' filtering.","summary":"comments_read shows a withheld anchor's file as index.html","tags":["visibility","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:09.795162Z","id":"b7f24ef98974dfb949341d6ba66f1baa4ec194e102ab719ddd9ad6ef430949f5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f44be2c","summary":"Fixed: thread_summary gives a withheld anchor no file and no summary and carries anchor_withheld, clip_withheld, each comment's withheld flag and the thread's withheld summary. Test: cargo test -p clax-mcp --lib a_thread_summary_keeps_withheld_fields_withheld passes; api_visibility::mcp_tools_are_filtered_for_the_owner passes.","supersedes":"8bd3a5dd80c39c3894d638d0d133c7b5d69653c3624ef606ea9bccdf08f95e67","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T15:45:51.492804Z","id":"4b4a862fbd01266f56a6471c08566fb80ed3d8978c867fedae8cbbb97479fba8","body":{"detail":"Failure: a remote daemon puts clip_path \"/Users/sam/.clax/remote.key\" (or ~/.ssh/id_ed25519) on a thread; comments_read and the feedback payload's `Clip:` line hand it to the agent, whose tool description says to view the clip with its file tools, so the agent reads a local secret into its context. A daemon serving a grant never sends clip_path (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:520 only with the token), so any path from a remote daemon is foreign. Plan Task 19 rewrites remote clip lines to cached files.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":585},"end":{"line":610},"content_hash":"e5ad9f7463b428b2b184731654cc20f56c86793209b057a750f70798b912f9bc"},"suggested_fix":"In Task 19's rewrite, never pass a remote clip_path or snapshot_path through: replace it with the fetched file under <home>/remote-cache/clips/ or `Clip: unavailable (…)`.","summary":"In remote mode the agent is shown whatever clip path the remote daemon sends, as a file to open","tags":["security","review","revisit:Task 19 remote clip rewrite","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/shim.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T16:50:12.003938Z","id":"09424caedb6427bd7d18c7e2095a0865f3a3ea75ddb2f00e6f6df2f174650d79","body":{"detail":"Not taken (2026-10-01, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-01-grok-build.md:115 (Q2)): sandboxed Grok is unsupported unless a daemon already runs; under the workspace, read-only and strict profiles a daemon the shim starts cannot write ~/.clax (docs/contract.md:4203-4207). Supporting it needs sandbox detection in the shim and a daemon start outside the sandbox; the contract's Known-limitations entry then goes.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":201},"end":{"line":218},"content_hash":"8ad74131cff0e96c44a667e6a3d7aecd30ec5c516b2e0c49d35a42face7a17c9"},"summary":"Support Grok's sandbox: detect it in the shim and start the daemon outside it","supersedes":"7b5749bd659189973546d590ce7735c100bcab247f10b10d99fc6fae4018ce9e","tags":["revisit:Grok users run with the sandbox on and no daemon started outside it","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:37:11.638636Z","id":"03903a98e24585272ee2c89f8e32daf0dbf0883252391991ca464ea98da6f7a6","body":{"detail":"Failure: a shim holds session X (or finds X in its file), and the remote daemon has no row X (the machine reconnected to another daemon without clax connect --off, or the daemon's data was reset). The registration with X is 400 unknown_session from Identity::caller's own_session check, which is not proof_refused, so the loop returns the error without trying the file or no credential; every later call refreshes and fails the same way until the shim restarts. The SessionStart hook's join (crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs:459-476) stops the same way on a stale file from another daemon.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":530},"end":{"line":540},"content_hash":"502da82e4cf94e5e61dbd9f953d24bd305aed30374e33fc6fb08b0eb3ca77039"},"suggested_fix":"Treat 400 unknown_session like invalid_session_proof when choosing the next registration or join candidate.","summary":"A registration whose held or filed credential names a session the daemon does not know stops instead of trying the next candidate","tags":["review","spec:6.8","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:20.902153Z","id":"299bddff81cc21828b327be9e964a7bbc071cac5474f9d1ed828a540e38ce6c0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:903f2670","summary":"The shim's registration and the hook's join pass over a credential refused as 400 unknown_session as they do one refused as invalid_session_proof (credential_refused). Evidence: remote::a_credential_for_a_session_the_daemon_does_not_know_is_passed_over and hook::join_tests::a_found_credential_is_used_and_a_stale_one_dropped pass; the mutation dropping unknown_session is caught.","supersedes":"03903a98e24585272ee2c89f8e32daf0dbf0883252391991ca464ea98da6f7a6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.743099Z","id":"aa30ce24a864109463092446a5f07afc629e74d95195bfcf72fe4ed824217718","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9be93c11","summary":"A grant session's payload names its clip clax-clip:<artifact>/<thread>; the shim, hooks and Pi fetch it into <home>/remote-cache/clips/ and rewrite the line, and any other Clip: or Snapshot: value and any clip_path or snapshot_path from a remote daemon becomes unavailable or null (clax_core::clips). Evidence: clips::tests::*, remote::remote_clip_lines_are_rewritten_to_cached_files and connect::remote_hooks_find_their_session pass; the shim test fails with the rewrite off.","supersedes":"4b4a862fbd01266f56a6471c08566fb80ed3d8978c867fedae8cbbb97479fba8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:02:04.319529Z","id":"6a33fedc3bc1f05db65d1e8b67287da978958c8e5caf01876efe48f5ca71c666","body":{"detail":"clip_bytes here, Client::get_bytes_with (crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs:978-989) and Pi's DaemonClient.clipBytes (plugins/pi/src/client.ts) buffer the whole response, and clax_core::clips::store / Pi's storeClip write it to <home>/remote-cache/clips/<aid>-<tid>.png. clips.rs treats a remote daemon as untrusted for paths (it never passes one through), but a hostile or broken daemon can answer a clip GET with gigabytes: the shim, hook or Pi process grows until it is killed and fills the cache disk. Content-Type is not checked, so any bytes are handed to the agent's file tools as an image.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1169},"end":{"line":1180},"content_hash":"6e5f63621aa4954611320f7c927134ad3280706fd154357768d939fefac6c157"},"suggested_fix":"Cap the body (the daemon's own clip upload limit is the natural bound), refuse a non-image/png Content-Type, and rewrite either to `Clip: unavailable (…)`.","summary":"Remote clips are read whole into memory with no size cap and stored as .png whatever their type, in the shim, the hooks and Pi","tags":["review","remote","security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:02:04.319836Z","id":"e65e38868bca2de84279061ea4b09db817850b300eb5e3ffc578faff16b202b1","body":{"detail":"The daemon route is POST /api/sessions/<sid>/threads/<tid>/handoff and takes no artifact. An agent that passes artifact A with a thread ID from artifact B hands off B's thread and is answered {artifact_id: A, url: A's URL, thread: B's}. Pi's commentsHandoff (plugins/pi/src/clax.ts) does the same.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1600},"end":{"line":1627},"content_hash":"c323ff5b1c677601b0c220be54d5fe9469799088faba395f8358f6ca05d27e09"},"suggested_fix":"Check that the returned thread's artifact is the resolved one (400 invalid_args otherwise), or report the thread's own artifact.","summary":"comments_handoff resolves url_or_id but sends only the thread ID, so the result can name an artifact the thread is not on","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:55:01.443571Z","id":"0675d7aad833ea9466808918f2855b128fdbfec4bcdefb0330c4b3f80b1d305e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7a06e2cd","summary":"Clip bodies are read to at most clax_core::clips::MAX_BYTES (+1) and must be image/png with a PNG signature before they are stored, in the shim (chunked read), the hook (Client::get_bytes_with streaming with a cap) and Pi (maxBytes, checkClip). Evidence: clips::tests::a_clip_is_checked_before_it_is_kept and Pi's 'a clip that does not come in time, or is not a PNG ...' (Clip: unavailable (not a PNG)) pass. A signed remote response is still read under the transport's 128 MiB cap before the clip check in the shim.","supersedes":"6a33fedc3bc1f05db65d1e8b67287da978958c8e5caf01876efe48f5ca71c666","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:55:01.445771Z","id":"ef7f194e70806d8c8da11284003348631217a29e0b814cbb922fe386635cbab3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7a06e2cd","summary":"comments_handoff first reads the thread on the named artifact (404 not_found otherwise), in the Rust tools and Pi. Evidence: people::comments_handoff_moves_and_releases and Pi's 'comments_handoff hands a thread to another agent by name and releases it' pass with a wrong-artifact case; without the read the Rust test fails.","supersedes":"e65e38868bca2de84279061ea4b09db817850b300eb5e3ffc578faff16b202b1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:16:36.712174Z","id":"f0839cd6725d0aa7faba03301b85434f61189c335bfcf31c0955bfbc9c92d5d2","body":{"detail":"For a remote daemon, DaemonClient::send goes through attempt_signed (crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs:1555-1645), which buffers the body through capped_body (:1648) before returning a reqwest::Response built from those bytes. clip_bytes' chunk loop then walks an in-memory body, so its break past clax_core::clips::MAX_BYTES only discards bytes already held. fetch_clips (:1241) spawns one task per distinct clip with no limit, so a hostile or broken remote daemon answering N clip requests with 128 MiB each holds N x 128 MiB in the shim for up to CLIP_FETCH_TIME (5 s); a daemon on the same host or a fast LAN can deliver that. The remote daemon can already return 128 MiB on any one request, so the change is the multiplication by N.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1186},"end":{"line":1205},"content_hash":"429cca002671ba4f1fb79f3b58f553950f384f854d9d382adcd596db194efda5"},"suggested_fix":"Give attempt_signed a per-call body limit (MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES by default, clips::MAX_BYTES + 1 for clip_bytes), refuse a Content-Length over it before reading, and run at most a few clip fetches at once (for example 4).","summary":"The shim's 5 MiB clip cap does not bound memory for a remote daemon: attempt_signed reads every answer whole (capped_body, up to MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES = 128 MiB) before clip_bytes sees a chunk, and fetch_clips runs every distinct clip at once","tags":["review","remote","security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:16:36.714218Z","id":"32facc1ab6b6b6d4f99192c25d24e58afc03a4b49f94d079d5df5c0d6ec3d05c","body":{"detail":"Mutations: an await of each JoinSet task right after it is spawned in fetch_clips survived remote::a_remote_clip_that_does_not_come_never_holds_the_feedback; Pi's fetchAll restored to its sequential loop survived all 104 vitest tests. Both tests assert the comments and the timed-out lines but no upper bound on the call, so N slow clips taking N x CLIP_FETCH_TIME would pass. In the hook, lifting fetch_within's wait (recv_timeout(left + 3600 s)) is killed only by clips::tests::fetches_are_deduplicated_concurrent_and_bounded: connect::a_remote_hook_prints_its_comments_when_clips_do_not_come still passes, because each fetch's reqwest timeout (with_timeout(left)) also ends the held request. The resolve of the I1 record (ed38a814) says the hook test fails with the bound lifted, which holds only if both bounds are lifted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1241},"end":{"line":1281},"content_hash":"9619e3d837193a08c6c5fe19fb4b3bb129dccd5ab07e115fdf0903b0991049d4"},"suggested_fix":"With two held clips and a fetch bound of t, assert the shim's and Pi's call returns in well under 2t (for example under 1.5t, with t large enough that scheduling noise stays small).","summary":"Fetching clips at once is untested in the shim and in Pi: a sequential fetch_clips, and a sequential fetchAll in plugins/pi/src/remote.ts, each pass every test","tags":["review","tests","remote","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:16:49.647738Z","id":"781337b262364c4fd32ec20730435a6adc97fa1dcc713129c1c18361914405f8","body":{"detail":"end_session sends PATCH {ended:true} through send_with; a remote daemon answers an ended session's proof with 401 invalid_session_proof, which attempt_signed marks refreshable (crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs:1628), so send_with (:706) re-registers a new row and ends that one. forget_credentials(&held) then removes only the old session's files, leaving the new session's credential file in remote-sessions/. Reproduced: shim registered (CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=sam-cc-12), `clax hook --agent claude session-end` ended it, the shim then closed: the sessions table holds a second row for sam-cc-12 named claude-4 (session.start and session.end in the journal, an 'ended' agent in the roster for an hour) and remote-sessions/claude-s-sam-cc-12.json names it. The local path makes no second row. Real Claude Code 2.1.301 -p did not hit it (its shim ended first). Pi's endSession (plugins/pi/src/client.ts:815) goes through the same refreshing json() path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1444},"end":{"line":1456},"content_hash":"668a763dee49a463b9a5ca2932acce68c84c0da726284a495b893a1e0e77e12a"},"suggested_fix":"Send the end without the re-registering retry (a non-refreshable send), treating invalid_session_proof and unknown_session as already ended.","summary":"end_session registers a new session when the held one has already ended, then ends it: a phantom session per exit after a SessionEnd hook (or People) ended the row","tags":["review","remote","lifecycle","final-review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:16:49.647857Z","id":"558a976788dd6c893a86be9c5ac28086be870478c3394a181fd5cf41344b65d7","body":{"detail":"A tool result's `withheld` entries are {thread_id, artifact_id, count, author, title, asked} with `author` the display name (crates/clax-core/src/feedback.rs:177-179; docs/contract.md:120-122). ask's description says `author` comes 'from the `withheld` summary', and its schema and docs/contract.md:2263 say 'the public ID a `withheld` summary names' - only comments_read's thread-level withheld.authors carries public_id. Driving the shim: ask {approval: {url_or_id, thread_id, author: \"Mia\"}} -> invalid_args 'author is a person's public ID'. The skill's own example ({\"thread_id\": ...}) works.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2564},"end":{"line":2564},"content_hash":"05dec516f95bb788e36b2e9b426958c3487badb93aff8850f90a55e2fbb08b5f"},"suggested_fix":"Add the author's public ID to the result-level withheld entries (e.g. author_id), or say in the description that `author` is the public_id from comments_read's withheld.authors.","summary":"ask tells the agent to pass the `author` the withheld summary names, but the result-level withheld summary names a display name and approval.author must be a public ID","tags":["review","remote","docs","final-review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/render.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:16:49.647897Z","id":"71fbd453fad78ac1377410d1bf7b12f0e3481cf7d3435969e2a6fde2dd038ff5","body":{"detail":"Reproduced: owner's daemon stopped, a remote shim's list call answered daemon_unreachable with log <home>/logs/daemon.log on the person's machine; the daemon and its log are on the owner's machine.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":129},"end":{"line":133},"content_hash":"4a9186d51595def129371ccd3a91ce6a7d4e59d9cff8753e2086eaafa4af1e12"},"suggested_fix":"In remote mode leave out `log` and say the owner's Clax at <url> does not answer (as the CLI's Unreachable does).","summary":"On a connected machine, daemon_unreachable says 'see its log' and names the local home's logs/daemon.log, which a remote-mode home never writes","tags":["review","remote","final-review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:10:27.143520Z","id":"5479e6b4c80926e154661b1848d6d6b9cf45e5946a6fc95d4e74f732961cd3ef","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:43aa4212","summary":"Fixed in 43aa4212: end_session (and Pi's endSession) treat unknown_session / invalid_session_proof as already ended and register nothing. Evidence: connect::a_remote_shim_ending_after_its_session_ended_makes_no_session passes (one session row, no credential file left; before: two rows for cc-ended); plugins/pi/test/remote.test.ts 'ending a session that already ended' passes (failed before the fix).","supersedes":"781337b262364c4fd32ec20730435a6adc97fa1dcc713129c1c18361914405f8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:10:27.145785Z","id":"9c4051a9f05da6f921fb250bfc69a00189c1e5bbfff46ff4b7287c41525c0a75","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c5f95b5b","summary":"Fixed in c5f95b5b: placeholders carry author_ids (public IDs) beside author (names); ask's description, docs/contract.md and the skills point approval.author at author_ids. Evidence: api_approvals::a_withheld_summary_names_the_public_ids_ask_takes passes (author 'Mia' -> invalid_args, author_ids[0] -> accepted).","supersedes":"558a976788dd6c893a86be9c5ac28086be870478c3394a181fd5cf41344b65d7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/render.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:10:27.148060Z","id":"24ce2713db63b7cf78980a45575da796abdd96a3e979f0b4e6b640a4f95aefdd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c5f95b5b","summary":"Fixed in c5f95b5b: in remote mode daemon_unreachable and timeout carry no log and say the daemon and its log are on the owner's machine (ClaxTools::daemon_log). Evidence: render::tests::an_unreachable_remote_daemon_names_no_local_log passes.","supersedes":"71fbd453fad78ac1377410d1bf7b12f0e3481cf7d3435969e2a6fde2dd038ff5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/shim.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.854332Z","id":"68af3c6da2377d5594c2dd653d0b9f242ed27e85702287f5181890ab9d6beac1","body":{"detail":"Not taken (2026-10-01, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-01-grok-build.md:115 (Q2)): sandboxed Grok is unsupported unless a daemon already runs; under the workspace, read-only and strict profiles a daemon the shim starts cannot write ~/.clax (docs/contract.md:4203-4207). Supporting it needs sandbox detection in the shim and a daemon start outside the sandbox; the contract's Known-limitations entry then goes.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":202},"end":{"line":219},"content_hash":"8ad74131cff0e96c44a667e6a3d7aecd30ec5c516b2e0c49d35a42face7a17c9"},"summary":"Support Grok's sandbox: detect it in the shim and start the daemon outside it","supersedes":"09424caedb6427bd7d18c7e2095a0865f3a3ea75ddb2f00e6f6df2f174650d79","tags":["revisit:Grok users run with the sandbox on and no daemon started outside it","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:49:19.121754Z","id":"28b94761d9f4896d66ec5eea13cbcac502c7176199ef068579f4849c0ba9b559","body":{"detail":"The native http_client (client.rs:239-248) sets redirect Policy::none so a signed request and its body never go to a URL a daemon names. reqwest's wasm32 client has no redirect policy and fetch follows redirects, so the wasm32 http_client (client.rs:250-258) loses that guarantee. Signed requests are refused on wasm32 (attempt_signed's stub), so only bearer-token requests are exposed. On the Worker the client should reach the router in-process rather than over fetch, which removes the question; until then, a fetch with redirect: manual would need a web-sys request.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":250},"end":{"line":258},"content_hash":"c8520a2a07b7d2a7c562f43c13fbac505c7bf72a942c5b30f72e7b21cacd1b33"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set's client follows redirects","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:49:19.122014Z","id":"f70a6eb712a58c1d8504bb0e09ea17717a250d95e82e3df5767dcc9c6b6b1b35","body":{"detail":"attempt_signed is a stub on wasm32 (client.rs:1358-1376): reqwest's wasm32 Response cannot be rebuilt from read bytes (no From<http::Response>), which the native retry loop needs. The local path still sends to DaemonClient's base URL over fetch; in a Durable Object that base is the object itself, so a tool call would loop out through the network. The Worker needs a DaemonClient transport that calls the server's Router in-process (tower Service::call), which also makes the futures Send again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1358},"end":{"line":1376},"content_hash":"27776cee3aecb06d38d58805b5a2f714b2ab340fd7e1753a2dde1e6d6326f856"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set reaches no remote daemon, and reaches its own over fetch","tags":["wasm","revisit:the Worker crate serves /mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:49:19.122756Z","id":"c886b55dac8905856315d397b88dee4369bf0837a9a14ba49a270d94f3e9618e","body":{"detail":"run_opener (tools.rs:2080-2106) and GitCapture::start (git.rs:78) take std::time::Instant::now, which panics on wasm32. Neither runs in a Worker today: a process spawn fails first in run_opener, and a Worker builds ClaxTools without with_git. A Worker's ClaxTools should set Opener::Off so the open tool never tries; gitctx's API takes std's Instant (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2090},"end":{"line":2090},"content_hash":"237e5f5a8a995be40595501dcdb62befa5bb7759b8115cf4144af1f1130bce8d"},"summary":"The open tool's opener and the git capture read std's clock, which panics on wasm32","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:29:02.660180Z","id":"0c6b65cc3d26c98145a04d61826939bf3e0eecd69bc5cb38711ad3066d88e83c","body":{"detail":"Failure: a remote daemon puts clip_path \"/Users/sam/.clax/remote.key\" (or ~/.ssh/id_ed25519) on a thread; comments_read and the feedback payload's `Clip:` line hand it to the agent, whose tool description says to view the clip with its file tools, so the agent reads a local secret into its context. A daemon serving a grant never sends clip_path (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:520 only with the token), so any path from a remote daemon is foreign. Plan Task 19 rewrites remote clip lines to cached files.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":604},"end":{"line":629},"content_hash":"e5ad9f7463b428b2b184731654cc20f56c86793209b057a750f70798b912f9bc"},"suggested_fix":"In Task 19's rewrite, never pass a remote clip_path or snapshot_path through: replace it with the fetched file under <home>/remote-cache/clips/ or `Clip: unavailable (…)`.","summary":"In remote mode the agent is shown whatever clip path the remote daemon sends, as a file to open","supersedes":"4b4a862fbd01266f56a6471c08566fb80ed3d8978c867fedae8cbbb97479fba8","tags":["security","review","revisit:Task 19 remote clip rewrite","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.512326Z","id":"172ad7d6d4289d3e79b1b63e45a1dc6f34df5d3065eb2dc5ea4cfe291846edba","body":{"detail":"attempt_signed is a stub on wasm32 (client.rs:1358-1376): reqwest's wasm32 Response cannot be rebuilt from read bytes (no From<http::Response>), which the native retry loop needs. The local path still sends to DaemonClient's base URL over fetch; in a Durable Object that base is the object itself, so a tool call would loop out through the network. The Worker needs a DaemonClient transport that calls the server's Router in-process (tower Service::call), which also makes the futures Send again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1381},"end":{"line":1399},"content_hash":"27776cee3aecb06d38d58805b5a2f714b2ab340fd7e1753a2dde1e6d6326f856"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set reaches no remote daemon, and reaches its own over fetch","supersedes":"f70a6eb712a58c1d8504bb0e09ea17717a250d95e82e3df5767dcc9c6b6b1b35","tags":["wasm","revisit:the Worker crate serves /mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:01:18.516611Z","id":"9acaac79520deceb5351907796903339407bee8217c01e296862a6dbb7eed149","body":{"detail":"run_opener (tools.rs:2080-2106) and GitCapture::start (git.rs:78) take std::time::Instant::now, which panics on wasm32. Neither runs in a Worker today: a process spawn fails first in run_opener, and a Worker builds ClaxTools without with_git. A Worker's ClaxTools should set Opener::Off so the open tool never tries; gitctx's API takes std's Instant (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2196},"end":{"line":2196},"content_hash":"237e5f5a8a995be40595501dcdb62befa5bb7759b8115cf4144af1f1130bce8d"},"summary":"The open tool's opener and the git capture read std's clock, which panics on wasm32","supersedes":"c886b55dac8905856315d397b88dee4369bf0837a9a14ba49a270d94f3e9618e","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:00.449005Z","id":"eeebd55097761e6b7d43055ca232d4107c8646b7aab56038f02abfc3a169de3f","body":{"detail":"Failure: a remote daemon puts clip_path \"/Users/sam/.clax/remote.key\" (or ~/.ssh/id_ed25519) on a thread; comments_read and the feedback payload's `Clip:` line hand it to the agent, whose tool description says to view the clip with its file tools, so the agent reads a local secret into its context. A daemon serving a grant never sends clip_path (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:520 only with the token), so any path from a remote daemon is foreign. Plan Task 19 rewrites remote clip lines to cached files.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":587},"end":{"line":612},"content_hash":"e5ad9f7463b428b2b184731654cc20f56c86793209b057a750f70798b912f9bc"},"suggested_fix":"In Task 19's rewrite, never pass a remote clip_path or snapshot_path through: replace it with the fetched file under <home>/remote-cache/clips/ or `Clip: unavailable (…)`.","summary":"In remote mode the agent is shown whatever clip path the remote daemon sends, as a file to open","supersedes":"4b4a862fbd01266f56a6471c08566fb80ed3d8978c867fedae8cbbb97479fba8","tags":["security","review","revisit:Task 19 remote clip rewrite","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:00.456191Z","id":"96e5240333360949b2a0cef1971e69e37f66e320e01dc408302ac9faa6495a91","body":{"detail":"The native http_client (client.rs:239-248) sets redirect Policy::none so a signed request and its body never go to a URL a daemon names. reqwest's wasm32 client has no redirect policy and fetch follows redirects, so the wasm32 http_client (client.rs:250-258) loses that guarantee. Signed requests are refused on wasm32 (attempt_signed's stub), so only bearer-token requests are exposed. On the Worker the client should reach the router in-process rather than over fetch, which removes the question; until then, a fetch with redirect: manual would need a web-sys request.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":295},"end":{"line":303},"content_hash":"c8520a2a07b7d2a7c562f43c13fbac505c7bf72a942c5b30f72e7b21cacd1b33"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set's client follows redirects","supersedes":"28b94761d9f4896d66ec5eea13cbcac502c7176199ef068579f4849c0ba9b559","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:00.462643Z","id":"25816b741c6993742623484bdeece98188c7b9d1724dfa446c73fc631d656d5b","body":{"detail":"run_opener (tools.rs:2080-2106) and GitCapture::start (git.rs:78) take std::time::Instant::now, which panics on wasm32. Neither runs in a Worker today: a process spawn fails first in run_opener, and a Worker builds ClaxTools without with_git. A Worker's ClaxTools should set Opener::Off so the open tool never tries; gitctx's API takes std's Instant (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2147},"end":{"line":2147},"content_hash":"237e5f5a8a995be40595501dcdb62befa5bb7759b8115cf4144af1f1130bce8d"},"summary":"The open tool's opener and the git capture read std's clock, which panics on wasm32","supersedes":"c886b55dac8905856315d397b88dee4369bf0837a9a14ba49a270d94f3e9618e","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:00.597618Z","id":"20e4e214e462989af7cd594458c2a8a4181bb36c8beda981522526370ce77832","body":{"detail":"attempt_signed is a stub on wasm32 (client.rs:1358-1376): reqwest's wasm32 Response cannot be rebuilt from read bytes (no From<http::Response>), which the native retry loop needs. The local path still sends to DaemonClient's base URL over fetch; in a Durable Object that base is the object itself, so a tool call would loop out through the network. The Worker needs a DaemonClient transport that calls the server's Router in-process (tower Service::call), which also makes the futures Send again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1419},"end":{"line":1433},"content_hash":"00e61525e8ff8e7ec2c24745bd93e13a65f171cac8f1ac14075b5efb6f559b01"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set reaches no remote daemon, and reaches its own over fetch","supersedes":"f70a6eb712a58c1d8504bb0e09ea17717a250d95e82e3df5767dcc9c6b6b1b35","tags":["wasm","revisit:the Worker crate serves /mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:55.452046Z","id":"6b4375b8d2ab15b2f8ea788de623d62f78edc6362141fec121c0e299227a0545","body":{"detail":"rmcp's service validates SEP-2243's Mcp-Method and Mcp-Param-* headers against the body (validate_standard_headers in rmcp 3.5's transport/streamable_http_server/tower.rs) and refuses a mismatch with HTTP 400 / -32020. check_headers here checks only MCP-Protocol-Version (known version, match with initialize's params, match with _meta's protocolVersion). So a request whose Mcp-Method header names another method than its body is refused by /mcp and answered by /mcp/json. Clients send matching headers (crates/clax-server/tests/fixtures/claude_code_mcp_http.json), so the parity test passes; a malformed client would see the two differ.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":297},"end":{"line":352},"content_hash":"8025adc175b892391e681bcdfd077d59c4e7b97678cafeab9defc36f0ac5f491"},"summary":"The adapter does not check the 2026-07-28 standard headers rmcp checks","tags":["mcp","parity","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:55.452259Z","id":"ef63fa6e4aedba86a975991063df7111e10d94eba3159c47576b8955bc6e3a45","body":{"detail":"The version rules (inline negotiation, required _meta, legacy lifecycle for ping, resultType stripped before 2026-07-28), the tools/list cache hints, and the defaults for completion/complete, prompts/list, resources/list and resources/templates/list are copies of rmcp 3.5.0's handler/server.rs and rmcp-macros' tool_handler, because ServerHandler::handle_request needs a RequestContext whose Peer only rmcp can build. negotiate_initialize, DiscoverResult::from_server_info, ClaxTools::tools and the tool methods are called, not copied. crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp_http.rs the_adapter_answers_as_rmcp_does compares the two endpoints message by message and is what catches a divergence after an upgrade.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":373},"end":{"line":464},"content_hash":"4bb76252ad4228d2a1b0c5eda11bda944df97e84e06fe863d0c416023ff27a02"},"summary":"dispatch restates rmcp 3.5's server handler, so an rmcp upgrade can change /mcp without /mcp/json","tags":["mcp","parity","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:55.453025Z","id":"68e20d8f448ef646d94821661312d59f73d59de0de6111ac9bee4d2980e3a0a8","body":{"detail":"rmcp answers 406 unless Accept lists both application/json and text/event-stream (handle_post in rmcp 3.5's tower.rs). The adapter only ever answers application/json, so it admits any Accept that allows JSON (application/json, application/*, */*) or no Accept header, and answers 406 to one that does not (crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp_http.rs the_adapter_follows_the_http_rules_of_a_stateless_server). Every client that works with /mcp works here.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":103},"end":{"line":116},"content_hash":"c501ef96dd7c573bdd6bfe2166aa7715f745f892302b2f1f3fa50e1419628cf2"},"summary":"The adapter accepts a POST whose Accept admits only JSON, which rmcp's service refuses","tags":["mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:55.453418Z","id":"e51b2350c9922aaf742c30e325d4b5ee669f9b6b20cba9d3a327213a3c7c4d0a","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the adapter is stateless and issues no session. The daemon's /mcp tools act as the sessionless agent whatever rmcp session a client holds (DaemonClient::new with no session in crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp.rs and mcp_http.rs), so a session ID would name nothing. Claude Code 2.1.296 (recorded exchange in crates/clax-server/tests/fixtures/claude_code_mcp_http.json) uses the per-request lifecycle and sends none; rmcp's Streamable HTTP client, which Codex embeds, has allow_stateless on by default and works against /mcp/json (rmcps_client_works_on_both_endpoints). The prototype's session maps to an agent registration (a harness session) per MCP client; Clax's sessions come from the shim's registration instead.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":30},"content_hash":"1484b7bf6af20a25e6ea5684e30237e5222312c150ee0e0271d2211b489473d1"},"summary":"Signed, storage-free Mcp-Session-Id values (an HMAC of the agent and a generation under the token, as hosted/src/mcp/session.ts makes them)","tags":["mcp","revisit:a client refuses a server that issues no Mcp-Session-Id, or the hosted /mcp registers a harness session per MCP client as the prototype does","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:55.455134Z","id":"d8a94510fbe87e898b4f152ac75ef75873b04a01881ae368c46fb227dbdd13c6","body":{"detail":"attempt_in_process (crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs) hands each request to an InProcess transport; crates/clax-server/src/loopback.rs implements it over the whole router, and crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs builds the adapter's tools with it on both targets. The remote half (attempt_signed's wasm32 stub) is unchanged. Once the Worker crate serves the adapter, the fetch-to-itself half can be closed.","kind":"comment","references":"20e4e214e462989af7cd594458c2a8a4181bb36c8beda981522526370ce77832","summary":"The in-process transport exists: DaemonClient::with_in_process and clax_server::loopback::Loopback","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:06:55.455217Z","id":"7cc19426b6c16e007d52528a683e8b6a8f3815cf2dbc237ef179fa037d145676","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs builds its DaemonClient with_in_process(Loopback), so no request of theirs follows a redirect. Only a wasm32 DaemonClient made without a transport still goes over fetch.","kind":"comment","references":"96e5240333360949b2a0cef1971e69e37f66e320e01dc408302ac9faa6495a91","summary":"The adapter's tools no longer use fetch: they reach the router in-process","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:15.434617Z","id":"bcb3e4d4a1cefcabec4774cfe9a40484bb4f4c93b50bdd772753dce36b908cf8","body":{"detail":"The native http_client (client.rs:239-248) sets redirect Policy::none so a signed request and its body never go to a URL a daemon names. reqwest's wasm32 client has no redirect policy and fetch follows redirects, so the wasm32 http_client (client.rs:250-258) loses that guarantee. Signed requests are refused on wasm32 (attempt_signed's stub), so only bearer-token requests are exposed. On the Worker the client should reach the router in-process rather than over fetch, which removes the question; until then, a fetch with redirect: manual would need a web-sys request.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":311},"end":{"line":319},"content_hash":"c8520a2a07b7d2a7c562f43c13fbac505c7bf72a942c5b30f72e7b21cacd1b33"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set's client follows redirects","supersedes":"96e5240333360949b2a0cef1971e69e37f66e320e01dc408302ac9faa6495a91","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:15.436806Z","id":"5691e889fb8f9ed4cc714fe71c100051637a8a933a05367c8c1c8df140d2b7ad","body":{"detail":"attempt_signed is a stub on wasm32 (client.rs:1358-1376): reqwest's wasm32 Response cannot be rebuilt from read bytes (no From<http::Response>), which the native retry loop needs. The local path still sends to DaemonClient's base URL over fetch; in a Durable Object that base is the object itself, so a tool call would loop out through the network. The Worker needs a DaemonClient transport that calls the server's Router in-process (tower Service::call), which also makes the futures Send again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1459},"end":{"line":1473},"content_hash":"00e61525e8ff8e7ec2c24745bd93e13a65f171cac8f1ac14075b5efb6f559b01"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set reaches no remote daemon, and reaches its own over fetch","supersedes":"20e4e214e462989af7cd594458c2a8a4181bb36c8beda981522526370ce77832","tags":["wasm","revisit:the Worker crate serves /mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:15.438768Z","id":"b7dd52605e3f06825ed0934a1e94add0c6b8510654fe40408b48c06e204729bc","body":{"detail":"rmcp's service validates SEP-2243's Mcp-Method and Mcp-Param-* headers against the body (validate_standard_headers in rmcp 3.5's transport/streamable_http_server/tower.rs) and refuses a mismatch with HTTP 400 / -32020. check_headers here checks only MCP-Protocol-Version (known version, match with initialize's params, match with _meta's protocolVersion). So a request whose Mcp-Method header names another method than its body is refused by /mcp and answered by /mcp/json. Clients send matching headers (crates/clax-server/tests/fixtures/claude_code_mcp_http.json), so the parity test passes; a malformed client would see the two differ.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":286},"end":{"line":341},"content_hash":"8025adc175b892391e681bcdfd077d59c4e7b97678cafeab9defc36f0ac5f491"},"summary":"The adapter does not check the 2026-07-28 standard headers rmcp checks","supersedes":"6b4375b8d2ab15b2f8ea788de623d62f78edc6362141fec121c0e299227a0545","tags":["mcp","parity","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:15.440673Z","id":"1779e8e13b0ae9e1c227d22d0d9a924ac5ad58474705411fd35c1558a890cd08","body":{"detail":"The version rules (inline negotiation, required _meta, legacy lifecycle for ping, resultType stripped before 2026-07-28), the tools/list cache hints, and the defaults for completion/complete, prompts/list, resources/list and resources/templates/list are copies of rmcp 3.5.0's handler/server.rs and rmcp-macros' tool_handler, because ServerHandler::handle_request needs a RequestContext whose Peer only rmcp can build. negotiate_initialize, DiscoverResult::from_server_info, ClaxTools::tools and the tool methods are called, not copied. crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp_http.rs the_adapter_answers_as_rmcp_does compares the two endpoints message by message and is what catches a divergence after an upgrade.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":362},"end":{"line":453},"content_hash":"4bb76252ad4228d2a1b0c5eda11bda944df97e84e06fe863d0c416023ff27a02"},"summary":"dispatch restates rmcp 3.5's server handler, so an rmcp upgrade can change /mcp without /mcp/json","supersedes":"ef63fa6e4aedba86a975991063df7111e10d94eba3159c47576b8955bc6e3a45","tags":["mcp","parity","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:15.442549Z","id":"ce072f823a8141ddfd4686864628a6b2e2e25ec98f616316f6da8675325fd4e2","body":{"detail":"rmcp answers 406 unless Accept lists both application/json and text/event-stream (handle_post in rmcp 3.5's tower.rs). The adapter only ever answers application/json, so it admits any Accept that allows JSON (application/json, application/*, */*) or no Accept header, and answers 406 to one that does not (crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp_http.rs the_adapter_follows_the_http_rules_of_a_stateless_server). Every client that works with /mcp works here.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":105},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"c501ef96dd7c573bdd6bfe2166aa7715f745f892302b2f1f3fa50e1419628cf2"},"summary":"The adapter accepts a POST whose Accept admits only JSON, which rmcp's service refuses","supersedes":"68e20d8f448ef646d94821661312d59f73d59de0de6111ac9bee4d2980e3a0a8","tags":["mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/http.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:15.444417Z","id":"9de391b42684914e6806585adb746dae12cc9f6e21fcf92b5f3572afb86c0e2c","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the adapter is stateless and issues no session. The daemon's /mcp tools act as the sessionless agent whatever rmcp session a client holds (DaemonClient::new with no session in crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp.rs and mcp_http.rs), so a session ID would name nothing. Claude Code 2.1.296 (recorded exchange in crates/clax-server/tests/fixtures/claude_code_mcp_http.json) uses the per-request lifecycle and sends none; rmcp's Streamable HTTP client, which Codex embeds, has allow_stateless on by default and works against /mcp/json (rmcps_client_works_on_both_endpoints). The prototype's session maps to an agent registration (a harness session) per MCP client; Clax's sessions come from the shim's registration instead.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"afd5cc09fd5e51f945bdeea175e66435172a6344bdd26db2817e1c916eb478ef"},"summary":"Signed, storage-free Mcp-Session-Id values (an HMAC of the agent and a generation under the token, as hosted/src/mcp/session.ts makes them)","supersedes":"e51b2350c9922aaf742c30e325d4b5ee669f9b6b20cba9d3a327213a3c7c4d0a","tags":["mcp","revisit:a client refuses a server that issues no Mcp-Session-Id, or the hosted /mcp registers a harness session per MCP client as the prototype does","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:38:15.446651Z","id":"1b9e00524f5863db3d3bf27f17b63b21be10dc17c07686c6eefb0c2053eb3827","body":{"detail":"run_opener (tools.rs:2080-2106) and GitCapture::start (git.rs:78) take std::time::Instant::now, which panics on wasm32. Neither runs in a Worker today: a process spawn fails first in run_opener, and a Worker builds ClaxTools without with_git. A Worker's ClaxTools should set Opener::Off so the open tool never tries; gitctx's API takes std's Instant (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2160},"end":{"line":2160},"content_hash":"237e5f5a8a995be40595501dcdb62befa5bb7759b8115cf4144af1f1130bce8d"},"summary":"The open tool's opener and the git capture read std's clock, which panics on wasm32","supersedes":"25816b741c6993742623484bdeece98188c7b9d1724dfa446c73fc631d656d5b","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:46:07.718271Z","id":"e961fde23ff3c08b68c69eb0f02acef26113deb1b3f48fc1514202c71dacc431","body":{"detail":"Failure: a remote daemon puts clip_path \"/Users/sam/.clax/remote.key\" (or ~/.ssh/id_ed25519) on a thread; comments_read and the feedback payload's `Clip:` line hand it to the agent, whose tool description says to view the clip with its file tools, so the agent reads a local secret into its context. A daemon serving a grant never sends clip_path (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:520 only with the token), so any path from a remote daemon is foreign. Plan Task 19 rewrites remote clip lines to cached files.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":606},"end":{"line":631},"content_hash":"e5ad9f7463b428b2b184731654cc20f56c86793209b057a750f70798b912f9bc"},"suggested_fix":"In Task 19's rewrite, never pass a remote clip_path or snapshot_path through: replace it with the fetched file under <home>/remote-cache/clips/ or `Clip: unavailable (…)`.","summary":"In remote mode the agent is shown whatever clip path the remote daemon sends, as a file to open","supersedes":"0c6b65cc3d26c98145a04d61826939bf3e0eecd69bc5cb38711ad3066d88e83c","tags":["security","review","revisit:Task 19 remote clip rewrite","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:46:07.722115Z","id":"2e5d5f0ecf72bf7674a161f6aa31906c35414d95638d25dfd8df9f430e974878","body":{"detail":"run_opener (tools.rs:2080-2106) and GitCapture::start (git.rs:78) take std::time::Instant::now, which panics on wasm32. Neither runs in a Worker today: a process spawn fails first in run_opener, and a Worker builds ClaxTools without with_git. A Worker's ClaxTools should set Opener::Off so the open tool never tries; gitctx's API takes std's Instant (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2266},"end":{"line":2266},"content_hash":"237e5f5a8a995be40595501dcdb62befa5bb7759b8115cf4144af1f1130bce8d"},"summary":"The open tool's opener and the git capture read std's clock, which panics on wasm32","supersedes":"9acaac79520deceb5351907796903339407bee8217c01e296862a6dbb7eed149","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:16:47.746023Z","id":"97d5883f8233ecd66751458c5c111f7c3be3643000e1a695af2e2fe424a62332","body":{"detail":"The token is handed to the session (its holder, whose pushes are its person's), so the tool calls POST /api/sessions/<sid>/git-token/<id>. Over /mcp and /mcp/json (crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp.rs mcp_git_remote_without_a_session_is_no_session) there is no session; an agent reaches the Worker's git remotes only through the stdio shim's registered session, as draft does.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1865},"end":{"line":1888},"content_hash":"6df2f80cf2864a4d7dd95b0e9c8e4c20238357f09b3d99a324a8e639c620509c"},"summary":"git_remote needs a harness session, so it answers no_session over the /mcp endpoints, which have none","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:25.934940Z","id":"78a11a895e56d258156e62aefffb8e63bd5f9c9d0059d24fc4766cb8a778a83e","body":{"detail":"attempt_signed is a stub on wasm32 (client.rs:1358-1376): reqwest's wasm32 Response cannot be rebuilt from read bytes (no From<http::Response>), which the native retry loop needs. The local path still sends to DaemonClient's base URL over fetch; in a Durable Object that base is the object itself, so a tool call would loop out through the network. The Worker needs a DaemonClient transport that calls the server's Router in-process (tower Service::call), which also makes the futures Send again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1394},"end":{"line":1412},"content_hash":"6bab3334852699f5ef4775797dec0c99654f0e0522550af12a2b0cfba43ce9fc"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set reaches no remote daemon, and reaches its own over fetch","supersedes":"172ad7d6d4289d3e79b1b63e45a1dc6f34df5d3065eb2dc5ea4cfe291846edba","tags":["wasm","revisit:the Worker crate serves /mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:25.939347Z","id":"3031db8c8b8b99c7982b780023470b53259c9244e239daee110052fe64fd3640","body":{"detail":"attempt_signed is a stub on wasm32 (client.rs:1358-1376): reqwest's wasm32 Response cannot be rebuilt from read bytes (no From<http::Response>), which the native retry loop needs. The local path still sends to DaemonClient's base URL over fetch; in a Durable Object that base is the object itself, so a tool call would loop out through the network. The Worker needs a DaemonClient transport that calls the server's Router in-process (tower Service::call), which also makes the futures Send again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1472},"end":{"line":1486},"content_hash":"374bf4260aa8a5eb77a52f0a9fba75b806aff3c83311a283b9b306f7570d8e4b"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set reaches no remote daemon, and reaches its own over fetch","supersedes":"5691e889fb8f9ed4cc714fe71c100051637a8a933a05367c8c1c8df140d2b7ad","tags":["wasm","revisit:the Worker crate serves /mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:25.943530Z","id":"efd65ac398d52dbe7d3dcf4f2c9b44863b29384baf5d4b1ee08088d1828f565a","body":{"detail":"Failure: a remote daemon puts clip_path \"/Users/sam/.clax/remote.key\" (or ~/.ssh/id_ed25519) on a thread; comments_read and the feedback payload's `Clip:` line hand it to the agent, whose tool description says to view the clip with its file tools, so the agent reads a local secret into its context. A daemon serving a grant never sends clip_path (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:520 only with the token), so any path from a remote daemon is foreign. Plan Task 19 rewrites remote clip lines to cached files.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":606},"end":{"line":631},"content_hash":"e94a00b2e295f6f7500afc47732651840be708ff39c555c72b72dbffaba0fe69"},"suggested_fix":"In Task 19's rewrite, never pass a remote clip_path or snapshot_path through: replace it with the fetched file under <home>/remote-cache/clips/ or `Clip: unavailable (…)`.","summary":"In remote mode the agent is shown whatever clip path the remote daemon sends, as a file to open","supersedes":"eeebd55097761e6b7d43055ca232d4107c8646b7aab56038f02abfc3a169de3f","tags":["security","review","revisit:Task 19 remote clip rewrite","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:25.947731Z","id":"48487ad381126d635caea3ea6632e68cc99ca486c319f1b52acd3b14e5bf3421","body":{"detail":"Failure: a remote daemon puts clip_path \"/Users/sam/.clax/remote.key\" (or ~/.ssh/id_ed25519) on a thread; comments_read and the feedback payload's `Clip:` line hand it to the agent, whose tool description says to view the clip with its file tools, so the agent reads a local secret into its context. A daemon serving a grant never sends clip_path (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:520 only with the token), so any path from a remote daemon is foreign. Plan Task 19 rewrites remote clip lines to cached files.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":625},"end":{"line":650},"content_hash":"e5ad9f7463b428b2b184731654cc20f56c86793209b057a750f70798b912f9bc"},"suggested_fix":"In Task 19's rewrite, never pass a remote clip_path or snapshot_path through: replace it with the fetched file under <home>/remote-cache/clips/ or `Clip: unavailable (…)`.","summary":"In remote mode the agent is shown whatever clip path the remote daemon sends, as a file to open","supersedes":"e961fde23ff3c08b68c69eb0f02acef26113deb1b3f48fc1514202c71dacc431","tags":["security","review","revisit:Task 19 remote clip rewrite","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:25.951919Z","id":"813e279b02f76cdcd44daa565efbb2066beaee2590d4e6432bec5f60fe9c150f","body":{"detail":"run_opener (tools.rs:2080-2106) and GitCapture::start (git.rs:78) take std::time::Instant::now, which panics on wasm32. Neither runs in a Worker today: a process spawn fails first in run_opener, and a Worker builds ClaxTools without with_git. A Worker's ClaxTools should set Opener::Off so the open tool never tries; gitctx's API takes std's Instant (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2310},"end":{"line":2310},"content_hash":"237e5f5a8a995be40595501dcdb62befa5bb7759b8115cf4144af1f1130bce8d"},"summary":"The open tool's opener and the git capture read std's clock, which panics on wasm32","supersedes":"2e5d5f0ecf72bf7674a161f6aa31906c35414d95638d25dfd8df9f430e974878","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:20:35.503271Z","id":"fee3d1759d2bd9ac707a7deff907146353604928ffcc52a6da56f156e6fd6df0","body":{"detail":"run_opener (tools.rs:2080-2106) and GitCapture::start (git.rs:78) take std::time::Instant::now, which panics on wasm32. Neither runs in a Worker today: a process spawn fails first in run_opener, and a Worker builds ClaxTools without with_git. A Worker's ClaxTools should set Opener::Off so the open tool never tries; gitctx's API takes std's Instant (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2161},"end":{"line":2161},"content_hash":"969994372cfe80832ac2a6e7db504a43dfa9d4929e58a11632ac746e78634048"},"summary":"The open tool's opener and the git capture read std's clock, which panics on wasm32","supersedes":"1b9e00524f5863db3d3bf27f17b63b21be10dc17c07686c6eefb0c2053eb3827","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.212985Z","id":"096227c014c9224d2602e4b86f089a647250b39cb172027bd849ba89a72a8e8a","body":{"detail":"Failure: a remote daemon puts clip_path \"/Users/sam/.clax/remote.key\" (or ~/.ssh/id_ed25519) on a thread; comments_read and the feedback payload's `Clip:` line hand it to the agent, whose tool description says to view the clip with its file tools, so the agent reads a local secret into its context. A daemon serving a grant never sends clip_path (crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:520 only with the token), so any path from a remote daemon is foreign. Plan Task 19 rewrites remote clip lines to cached files.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":614},"end":{"line":639},"content_hash":"e5ad9f7463b428b2b184731654cc20f56c86793209b057a750f70798b912f9bc"},"suggested_fix":"In Task 19's rewrite, never pass a remote clip_path or snapshot_path through: replace it with the fetched file under <home>/remote-cache/clips/ or `Clip: unavailable (…)`.","summary":"In remote mode the agent is shown whatever clip path the remote daemon sends, as a file to open","supersedes":"0c6b65cc3d26c98145a04d61826939bf3e0eecd69bc5cb38711ad3066d88e83c","tags":["security","review","revisit:Task 19 remote clip rewrite","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.216445Z","id":"f73a189d09eed6b8ca2ee6016fcb7eba06ef34253bcd99eb6e920cacdd6ed594","body":{"detail":"run_opener (tools.rs:2080-2106) and GitCapture::start (git.rs:78) take std::time::Instant::now, which panics on wasm32. Neither runs in a Worker today: a process spawn fails first in run_opener, and a Worker builds ClaxTools without with_git. A Worker's ClaxTools should set Opener::Off so the open tool never tries; gitctx's API takes std's Instant (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2227},"end":{"line":2227},"content_hash":"237e5f5a8a995be40595501dcdb62befa5bb7759b8115cf4144af1f1130bce8d"},"summary":"The open tool's opener and the git capture read std's clock, which panics on wasm32","supersedes":"9acaac79520deceb5351907796903339407bee8217c01e296862a6dbb7eed149","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:48:56.219888Z","id":"5ad2eaaac8b00cb1d296666ba5166d5bf69fcc50a259a7e1d14863a9e1f4a259","body":{"detail":"attempt_signed is a stub on wasm32 (client.rs:1358-1376): reqwest's wasm32 Response cannot be rebuilt from read bytes (no From<http::Response>), which the native retry loop needs. The local path still sends to DaemonClient's base URL over fetch; in a Durable Object that base is the object itself, so a tool call would loop out through the network. The Worker needs a DaemonClient transport that calls the server's Router in-process (tower Service::call), which also makes the futures Send again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1392},"end":{"line":1410},"content_hash":"27776cee3aecb06d38d58805b5a2f714b2ab340fd7e1753a2dde1e6d6326f856"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set reaches no remote daemon, and reaches its own over fetch","supersedes":"172ad7d6d4289d3e79b1b63e45a1dc6f34df5d3065eb2dc5ea4cfe291846edba","tags":["wasm","revisit:the Worker crate serves /mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.002386Z","id":"9c62e2a304ddf5506728dee1fdd9a252ede9b6a02e5da813044e182cb962b6e5","body":{"detail":"attempt_signed is a stub on wasm32 (client.rs:1358-1376): reqwest's wasm32 Response cannot be rebuilt from read bytes (no From<http::Response>), which the native retry loop needs. The local path still sends to DaemonClient's base URL over fetch; in a Durable Object that base is the object itself, so a tool call would loop out through the network. The Worker needs a DaemonClient transport that calls the server's Router in-process (tower Service::call), which also makes the futures Send again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1400},"end":{"line":1418},"content_hash":"6bab3334852699f5ef4775797dec0c99654f0e0522550af12a2b0cfba43ce9fc"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set reaches no remote daemon, and reaches its own over fetch","supersedes":"172ad7d6d4289d3e79b1b63e45a1dc6f34df5d3065eb2dc5ea4cfe291846edba","tags":["wasm","revisit:the Worker crate serves /mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.006578Z","id":"dcc16ccf7f2120b66bc470fd735a0715adf4c913b3074a2394a22fb6bb526056","body":{"detail":"The native http_client (client.rs:239-248) sets redirect Policy::none so a signed request and its body never go to a URL a daemon names. reqwest's wasm32 client has no redirect policy and fetch follows redirects, so the wasm32 http_client (client.rs:250-258) loses that guarantee. Signed requests are refused on wasm32 (attempt_signed's stub), so only bearer-token requests are exposed. On the Worker the client should reach the router in-process rather than over fetch, which removes the question; until then, a fetch with redirect: manual would need a web-sys request.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":316},"end":{"line":324},"content_hash":"c8520a2a07b7d2a7c562f43c13fbac505c7bf72a942c5b30f72e7b21cacd1b33"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set's client follows redirects","supersedes":"bcb3e4d4a1cefcabec4774cfe9a40484bb4f4c93b50bdd772753dce36b908cf8","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:21.010771Z","id":"78b208b64b5f24dd6c6f1ce7530f1161d103c405f896fe3ae5bfd1ba9c67cf72","body":{"detail":"attempt_signed is a stub on wasm32 (client.rs:1358-1376): reqwest's wasm32 Response cannot be rebuilt from read bytes (no From<http::Response>), which the native retry loop needs. The local path still sends to DaemonClient's base URL over fetch; in a Durable Object that base is the object itself, so a tool call would loop out through the network. The Worker needs a DaemonClient transport that calls the server's Router in-process (tower Service::call), which also makes the futures Send again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1478},"end":{"line":1492},"content_hash":"374bf4260aa8a5eb77a52f0a9fba75b806aff3c83311a283b9b306f7570d8e4b"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set reaches no remote daemon, and reaches its own over fetch","supersedes":"5691e889fb8f9ed4cc714fe71c100051637a8a933a05367c8c1c8df140d2b7ad","tags":["wasm","revisit:the Worker crate serves /mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
