{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:57:35.291551Z","id":"cbd157b17600a59281196cc376cf63c90b013ee3ba15d689bcf13a32df6c57ef","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"300029c169350d1f53c073cf195f10bdffa5ec12fd9e00eaf7cd10cea6f32055","summary":"Addressed in the working tree (not yet committed: commit signing failed): remote mode drops every clip_path and live snapshot_path a remote daemon sends and rewrites the payload's Clip:/Snapshot: lines (crates/clax-mcp/src/render.rs Handover::foreign, test a_remote_daemons_paths_are_never_handed_on; tools.rs summary_for_agent); linked threads cache clips under <home>/remote-cache/clips/ (crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs a_remote_clip_is_cached_here_and_no_remote_path_reaches_an_agent). Close with --ref once the commit lands.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T15:07:30.219893Z","id":"7e7bfa44ffdfe1e77e727938b64906fe13be26a20ce11261152a53098880463b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:add88e8f","summary":"Remote mode drops every clip_path and snapshot_path a remote daemon sends (crates/clax-mcp/src/render.rs), and linked threads cache clips under <home>/remote-cache/clips/. cargo test -p clax-mcp a_remote_daemons_paths_are_never_handed_on: 1 passed; cargo test -p clax-server --test integration a_remote_clip_is_cached_here_and_no_remote_path_reaches_an_agent: 1 passed.","supersedes":"300029c169350d1f53c073cf195f10bdffa5ec12fd9e00eaf7cd10cea6f32055","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/shim.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T03:29:07.909914Z","id":"83726fcb90c4fd2572da2290c4617eef0fa4f608234f6e4da692b5a31fd99ab5","body":{"detail":"With the launch flag present, forward_notices long-polls GET /api/sessions/<sid>/notices and the daemon stamps each notice it returns (Store::take_notices), so it is announced once across channel and follower (crates/clax-mcp/tests/channel.rs a_comment_is_announced_once_across_channel_and_follow). When organization policy, the --channels allowlist or the sign-in method refuses the channel, Claude Code drops each event silently, yet the notice is spent: a clax feedback follow the agent starts as a backup races the shim and usually prints nothing, and the daemon reports the session woken (its notices poll counts as a follower), so the page shows no 'won't be woken' mark. The wake block says sure: false and tells the agent to relaunch without the flag (crates/clax-core/src/wake.rs CHANNEL_DO).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":299},"end":{"line":330},"content_hash":"797b12175b00221b7ab3f473318a618148171edd210fbf483780115beb28af95"},"suggested_fix":"Mark the shim's poll as the channel's (for example ?via=channel) and have the daemon answer it empty while a non-channel follower of the session is connected, so a backup follower always wins; and count a channel poll as 'unsure' rather than woken in wakes_when_idle.","summary":"A channel Claude Code refused still takes every notice, so a follower started as a backup sees none","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/shim.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:24:24.162659Z","id":"e6934ed0eafbdbe9626701051bc7b3421862967b231240fa1fa2456dfa72b602","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:58380233","summary":"The shim polls notices with via=channel, and the daemon's notices route takes no notice for it while a follower of the session is connected (crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs, notices); a channel alone reads wakes \"unsure\". cargo test -p clax-server --test integration -- api_notices::a_channel_is_unsure_and_yields_its_notices_to_a_follower: ok","supersedes":"83726fcb90c4fd2572da2290c4617eef0fa4f608234f6e4da692b5a31fd99ab5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.365358Z","id":"a236613c100ecfbcee71ec878dffba562dfa789cc960302f6aba077c993d0ec8","body":{"detail":"The native http_client (client.rs:239-248) sets redirect Policy::none so a signed request and its body never go to a URL a daemon names. reqwest's wasm32 client has no redirect policy and fetch follows redirects, so the wasm32 http_client (client.rs:250-258) loses that guarantee. Signed requests are refused on wasm32 (attempt_signed's stub), so only bearer-token requests are exposed. On the Worker the client should reach the router in-process rather than over fetch, which removes the question; until then, a fetch with redirect: manual would need a web-sys request.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":364},"end":{"line":372},"content_hash":"c8520a2a07b7d2a7c562f43c13fbac505c7bf72a942c5b30f72e7b21cacd1b33"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set's client follows redirects","supersedes":"930bf2b7deee13fbef53134bb620006b1b3e383214da7c85e5807e388cc538c4","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.377821Z","id":"38654e703a7541208e7701b20c5c18aa4dedfff3470af8c3896ab08a95f0554b","body":{"detail":"Mutations: an await of each JoinSet task right after it is spawned in fetch_clips survived remote::a_remote_clip_that_does_not_come_never_holds_the_feedback; Pi's fetchAll restored to its sequential loop survived all 104 vitest tests. Both tests assert the comments and the timed-out lines but no upper bound on the call, so N slow clips taking N x CLIP_FETCH_TIME would pass. In the hook, lifting fetch_within's wait (recv_timeout(left + 3600 s)) is killed only by clips::tests::fetches_are_deduplicated_concurrent_and_bounded: connect::a_remote_hook_prints_its_comments_when_clips_do_not_come still passes, because each fetch's reqwest timeout (with_timeout(left)) also ends the held request. The resolve of the I1 record (ed38a814) says the hook test fails with the bound lifted, which holds only if both bounds are lifted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1554},"end":{"line":1594},"content_hash":"9619e3d837193a08c6c5fe19fb4b3bb129dccd5ab07e115fdf0903b0991049d4"},"suggested_fix":"With two held clips and a fetch bound of t, assert the shim's and Pi's call returns in well under 2t (for example under 1.5t, with t large enough that scheduling noise stays small).","summary":"Fetching clips at once is untested in the shim and in Pi: a sequential fetch_clips, and a sequential fetchAll in plugins/pi/src/remote.ts, each pass every test","supersedes":"32facc1ab6b6b6d4f99192c25d24e58afc03a4b49f94d079d5df5c0d6ec3d05c","tags":["review","tests","remote","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.390228Z","id":"b2c25739bfe32927583427386c7d76853e2c49101cfc9c6eaffa50af01c19409","body":{"detail":"attempt_signed is a stub on wasm32 (client.rs:1358-1376): reqwest's wasm32 Response cannot be rebuilt from read bytes (no From<http::Response>), which the native retry loop needs. The local path still sends to DaemonClient's base URL over fetch; in a Durable Object that base is the object itself, so a tool call would loop out through the network. The Worker needs a DaemonClient transport that calls the server's Router in-process (tower Service::call), which also makes the futures Send again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1916},"end":{"line":1934},"content_hash":"6bab3334852699f5ef4775797dec0c99654f0e0522550af12a2b0cfba43ce9fc"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set reaches no remote daemon, and reaches its own over fetch","supersedes":"9f6f5705635bfa01b245f3760802fc25a517c3e4cbcede1cc6b78b7ac1b6efd4","tags":["wasm","revisit:the Worker crate serves /mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.403271Z","id":"948236a860e50a9524a0f54ef4f703016f44544f7ec47338bac5a8689f5668eb","body":{"detail":"The token is handed to the session (its holder, whose pushes are its person's), so the tool calls POST /api/sessions/<sid>/git-token/<id>. Over /mcp and /mcp/json (crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp.rs mcp_git_remote_without_a_session_is_no_session) there is no session; an agent reaches the Worker's git remotes only through the stdio shim's registered session, as draft does.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2272},"end":{"line":2295},"content_hash":"6df2f80cf2864a4d7dd95b0e9c8e4c20238357f09b3d99a324a8e639c620509c"},"summary":"git_remote needs a harness session, so it answers no_session over the /mcp endpoints, which have none","supersedes":"0f5e32e3387a386a42fa097c7fbfde30a8904ca562ea06e6548a6c38fc104533","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.416318Z","id":"fd36a1394370a135a669f9ad9ea4fea8db92e6fdf188f931535c04194914cad1","body":{"detail":"run_opener (tools.rs:2080-2106) and GitCapture::start (git.rs:78) take std::time::Instant::now, which panics on wasm32. Neither runs in a Worker today: a process spawn fails first in run_opener, and a Worker builds ClaxTools without with_git. A Worker's ClaxTools should set Opener::Off so the open tool never tries; gitctx's API takes std's Instant (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2815},"end":{"line":2815},"content_hash":"237e5f5a8a995be40595501dcdb62befa5bb7759b8115cf4144af1f1130bce8d"},"summary":"The open tool's opener and the git capture read std's clock, which panics on wasm32","supersedes":"fcef9c8b407efa4381cd391cb9fcd317ecbbf6bcaebb7cecfad5047eb88653f3","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:19:13.429044Z","id":"65f6228b16333de8e45c20818ff512cafbe6e880ab66fca2324ce2ba65b40f93","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs:1186-1205, record f0839cd6. clip_bytes now reads through Reply::bytes_upto (line 328), which keeps at most clips::MAX_BYTES + 1 bytes, but for a remote daemon DaemonClient::send goes through attempt_signed (lines 1925-2017), which buffers the body through capped_body (line 2037) before returning a Reply, so the cap only discards bytes already held. fetch_clips (line 1554) spawns one task per distinct clip with no limit, so a hostile or broken remote daemon answering N clip requests with 128 MiB each holds N x 128 MiB in the shim for up to CLIP_FETCH_TIME (5 s); a daemon on the same host or a fast LAN can deliver that. The remote daemon can already return 128 MiB on any one request, so the change is the multiplication by N.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1491},"end":{"line":1507},"content_hash":"a41f8896c60cf22585325b9d454ad1c541da5cb976455798da00eaa960ca5e41"},"suggested_fix":"Give attempt_signed a per-call body limit (MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES by default, clips::MAX_BYTES + 1 for clip_bytes), refuse a Content-Length over it before reading, and run at most a few clip fetches at once (for example 4).","summary":"The shim's 5 MiB clip cap does not bound memory for a remote daemon: attempt_signed reads every answer whole (capped_body, up to MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES = 128 MiB) before clip_bytes' cap applies, and fetch_clips runs every distinct clip at once","supersedes":"f0839cd6725d0aa7faba03301b85434f61189c335bfcf31c0955bfbc9c92d5d2","tags":["review","remote","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:21:01.790105Z","id":"685efdfd2b71a6e616ec1c1fdc176691909e838add697ba35663786b3e67864c","body":{"detail":"ask's cancel results (do_ask's cancel arm, here; plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1594-1603) pass no suggestion to ask_result, and approval results (approval_result, crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:2473; plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1663) carry none. A cancel ends a question the agent is done with and an approval asks to see withheld content: neither answers where to ask the person next, and the feedback poll and question create and poll already carry the suggestion. Adding it would cost one GET /api/sessions/{id}/where-to-ask per call.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2373},"end":{"line":2390},"content_hash":"8142b2cc7646062309a4ca56e5d50d4b9c6b4f683beb18a3436a29d4b8f37f9c"},"summary":"Carry where_to_ask on ask's cancel and approval results too","tags":["revisit:an agent cancels an in-terminal question and then asks again without a fresh suggestion","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:21:01.829122Z","id":"fad473f284718af29e48f84fcdb2c5eb0618acb8fb7b503cbe44190e4b35bf2b","body":{"detail":"An ask with in_terminal: true takes the full question shape and validates it like any ask (clax_core::questions::validate_ask): options and all are stored and shown on the terminal card. Design spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md section 3 has the agent post only the headers; the tools do not enforce that, so a card may show options the person answers in the terminal.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2334},"end":{"line":2343},"content_hash":"1128a7b0ad9681a52d6f11203998da58eabf2877b57ed78701a184fe35d8353d"},"summary":"Limit an in-terminal ask to the questions' headers","tags":["revisit:terminal cards show options that read as answerable in Clax","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:38:49.800219Z","id":"c5c92612e6eaf61f98c73703fed1a9dda6606021e93e3986cd9cb87815a4c331","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"fad473f284718af29e48f84fcdb2c5eb0618acb8fb7b503cbe44190e4b35bf2b","summary":"The ask description (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:3261, plugins/pi/src/clax.ts, plugins/pi/test/fixtures/contract.json) now tells the agent to send each question's question and header only with in_terminal: true; the tools still accept and store full questions.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:16:44.620018Z","id":"149f25c34f7fffb830fd2238d61fc61c64a6d35da8e0bf5e8ddc8947573da942","body":{"detail":"ask_result sets surface_open (whether a Clax surface of the person was open when the question was created, remembered in ask_surface) on every open question asked in Clax; Pi's tool does the same (plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1726), and docs/contract.md:2857 describes it. Its only use for agents was the skills' 'If it also says surface_open: false, the person may not have Clax open' fallback to asking in chat too (plugins/*/skills/clax/SKILL.md at aa0696af3), which the skills dropped when they gained '## Where to ask': an agent asks on one surface and never mirrors the question in chat. The where_to_ask suggestion now tells the agent whether Clax can show a question. Question for the owner: drop surface_open from the ask result (and ask_surface with it), or keep it and document it as informational.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2581},"end":{"line":2586},"content_hash":"b56f74ba19edc23d7d456168cdd5d2da0b2b62745ca50442e42cca0040d6dce2"},"summary":"The ask result still carries surface_open for an open Clax question, but no agent instruction explains it any more","tags":["status:needs-decision","api","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.344168Z","id":"ee41662600054a04c19c432fa63c872b2a6f35cf5dbd0de44cae21089183f117","body":{"detail":"attempt_signed is a stub on wasm32 (client.rs:1358-1376): reqwest's wasm32 Response cannot be rebuilt from read bytes (no From<http::Response>), which the native retry loop needs. The local path still sends to DaemonClient's base URL over fetch; in a Durable Object that base is the object itself, so a tool call would loop out through the network. The Worker needs a DaemonClient transport that calls the server's Router in-process (tower Service::call), which also makes the futures Send again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1932},"end":{"line":1950},"content_hash":"6bab3334852699f5ef4775797dec0c99654f0e0522550af12a2b0cfba43ce9fc"},"summary":"On wasm32 the tool set reaches no remote daemon, and reaches its own over fetch","supersedes":"b2c25739bfe32927583427386c7d76853e2c49101cfc9c6eaffa50af01c19409","tags":["wasm","revisit:the Worker crate serves /mcp","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.366201Z","id":"80bc0d803cfc81c22ef7cca71d7d3c2c00acfc66195968240fff058b202e823e","body":{"detail":"The token is handed to the session (its holder, whose pushes are its person's), so the tool calls POST /api/sessions/<sid>/git-token/<id>. Over /mcp and /mcp/json (crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp.rs mcp_git_remote_without_a_session_is_no_session) there is no session; an agent reaches the Worker's git remotes only through the stdio shim's registered session, as draft does.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2289},"end":{"line":2312},"content_hash":"6df2f80cf2864a4d7dd95b0e9c8e4c20238357f09b3d99a324a8e639c620509c"},"summary":"git_remote needs a harness session, so it answers no_session over the /mcp endpoints, which have none","supersedes":"948236a860e50a9524a0f54ef4f703016f44544f7ec47338bac5a8689f5668eb","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.388360Z","id":"b85acb3838f6c6555c0086ce2edafdd805797e1b2a2c42ade38cd252687a3db8","body":{"detail":"run_opener (tools.rs:2080-2106) and GitCapture::start (git.rs:78) take std::time::Instant::now, which panics on wasm32. Neither runs in a Worker today: a process spawn fails first in run_opener, and a Worker builds ClaxTools without with_git. A Worker's ClaxTools should set Opener::Off so the open tool never tries; gitctx's API takes std's Instant (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2889},"end":{"line":2889},"content_hash":"237e5f5a8a995be40595501dcdb62befa5bb7759b8115cf4144af1f1130bce8d"},"summary":"The open tool's opener and the git capture read std's clock, which panics on wasm32","supersedes":"fd36a1394370a135a669f9ad9ea4fea8db92e6fdf188f931535c04194914cad1","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.410825Z","id":"f41bcee032daef5c38985ac7f9e82f2c0f355ad6fb3fefbfbdf30460d2bac5a2","body":{"detail":"ask's cancel results (do_ask's cancel arm, here; plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1594-1603) pass no suggestion to ask_result, and approval results (approval_result, crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:2473; plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1663) carry none. A cancel ends a question the agent is done with and an approval asks to see withheld content: neither answers where to ask the person next, and the feedback poll and question create and poll already carry the suggestion. Adding it would cost one GET /api/sessions/{id}/where-to-ask per call.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2393},"end":{"line":2410},"content_hash":"8142b2cc7646062309a4ca56e5d50d4b9c6b4f683beb18a3436a29d4b8f37f9c"},"summary":"Carry where_to_ask on ask's cancel and approval results too","supersedes":"685efdfd2b71a6e616ec1c1fdc176691909e838add697ba35663786b3e67864c","tags":["revisit:an agent cancels an in-terminal question and then asks again without a fresh suggestion","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.433572Z","id":"110f3202660b5e0ead943196351785249d33866b0d89284b48d73bfdfad19616","body":{"detail":"An ask with in_terminal: true takes the full question shape and validates it like any ask (clax_core::questions::validate_ask): options and all are stored and shown on the terminal card. Design spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md section 3 has the agent post only the headers; the tools do not enforce that, so a card may show options the person answers in the terminal.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2354},"end":{"line":2363},"content_hash":"1128a7b0ad9681a52d6f11203998da58eabf2877b57ed78701a184fe35d8353d"},"summary":"Limit an in-terminal ask to the questions' headers","supersedes":"fad473f284718af29e48f84fcdb2c5eb0618acb8fb7b503cbe44190e4b35bf2b","tags":["revisit:terminal cards show options that read as answerable in Clax","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.025387Z","id":"73a0dec97bc00ceba6cae9e7c7909ac91001902b109a50ffffa6375bd38514b1","body":{"detail":"do_ask creates the question and then waits in ask_wait for up to timeout_s (default 600 s; 50 s under Codex). tell_terminal (\"Asked in Clax: <url>\") is set only while the result's status is open, so it reaches the agent only after the wait runs out, never when the person answers within it; meanwhile the terminal shows the pending tool call (plugins/pi/src/clax.ts ask behaves the same). The skills' \"## Where to ask\" step 3 and INSTRUCTIONS say this as it is. Options: (a) the create returns at once with tell_terminal and call_again: true, and the agent writes the line and calls again with question_id; it works the same in all four harnesses; (b) the agent writes \"Asked in Clax: <place>\" in chat before calling ask (it knows the artifact and thread, not the browser base URL); (c) send the line as an MCP progress or log notification at create time, in harnesses that show those.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2323},"end":{"line":2430},"content_hash":"98f2e6809d1cbfeb1c376661b45a0d133ac3e4a218a329c714b46cda4a6ab0fe"},"summary":"Tell the terminal where a Clax question waits while ask is still waiting, rather than only in the result's tell_terminal after the wait","tags":["revisit:the owner picks (a), (b) or (c), or people report not knowing where a question waits","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.099048Z","id":"485d9c6573ae4b205cda0f967f5a2e207a6e22cecce1f241ec602b3b5566d7a4","body":{"detail":"The token is handed to the session (its holder, whose pushes are its person's), so the tool calls POST /api/sessions/<sid>/git-token/<id>. Over /mcp and /mcp/json (crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp.rs mcp_git_remote_without_a_session_is_no_session) there is no session; an agent reaches the Worker's git remotes only through the stdio shim's registered session, as draft does.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2290},"end":{"line":2313},"content_hash":"6df2f80cf2864a4d7dd95b0e9c8e4c20238357f09b3d99a324a8e639c620509c"},"summary":"git_remote needs a harness session, so it answers no_session over the /mcp endpoints, which have none","supersedes":"80bc0d803cfc81c22ef7cca71d7d3c2c00acfc66195968240fff058b202e823e","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.122844Z","id":"ffe18e7b92c41ac8d7e6dece94385f627555ed7889f317e3ded8765cd1882124","body":{"detail":"An ask with in_terminal: true takes the full question shape and validates it like any ask (clax_core::questions::validate_ask): options and all are stored and shown on the terminal card. Design spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md section 3 has the agent post only the headers; the tools do not enforce that, so a card may show options the person answers in the terminal.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2355},"end":{"line":2364},"content_hash":"1128a7b0ad9681a52d6f11203998da58eabf2877b57ed78701a184fe35d8353d"},"summary":"Limit an in-terminal ask to the questions' headers","supersedes":"110f3202660b5e0ead943196351785249d33866b0d89284b48d73bfdfad19616","tags":["revisit:terminal cards show options that read as answerable in Clax","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.146328Z","id":"2c48e2a8efea3e5aed5bbc3bf4993d93a75a35514ba59b3b2b3b993dedc25c48","body":{"detail":"ask's cancel results (do_ask's cancel arm, here; plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1594-1603) pass no suggestion to ask_result, and approval results (approval_result, crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:2473; plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1663) carry none. A cancel ends a question the agent is done with and an approval asks to see withheld content: neither answers where to ask the person next, and the feedback poll and question create and poll already carry the suggestion. Adding it would cost one GET /api/sessions/{id}/where-to-ask per call.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2394},"end":{"line":2411},"content_hash":"8142b2cc7646062309a4ca56e5d50d4b9c6b4f683beb18a3436a29d4b8f37f9c"},"summary":"Carry where_to_ask on ask's cancel and approval results too","supersedes":"f41bcee032daef5c38985ac7f9e82f2c0f355ad6fb3fefbfbdf30460d2bac5a2","tags":["revisit:an agent cancels an in-terminal question and then asks again without a fresh suggestion","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.169458Z","id":"ebf6dec5dc65a023edd7461b703f3e39c62ef4390ac6a2bd572e722d904cdbf0","body":{"detail":"ask_result sets surface_open (whether a Clax surface of the person was open when the question was created, remembered in ask_surface) on every open question asked in Clax; Pi's tool does the same (plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1726), and docs/contract.md:2857 describes it. Its only use for agents was the skills' 'If it also says surface_open: false, the person may not have Clax open' fallback to asking in chat too (plugins/*/skills/clax/SKILL.md at aa0696af3), which the skills dropped when they gained '## Where to ask': an agent asks on one surface and never mirrors the question in chat. The where_to_ask suggestion now tells the agent whether Clax can show a question. Question for the owner: drop surface_open from the ask result (and ask_surface with it), or keep it and document it as informational.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2582},"end":{"line":2587},"content_hash":"b56f74ba19edc23d7d456168cdd5d2da0b2b62745ca50442e42cca0040d6dce2"},"summary":"The ask result still carries surface_open for an open Clax question, but no agent instruction explains it any more","supersedes":"149f25c34f7fffb830fd2238d61fc61c64a6d35da8e0bf5e8ddc8947573da942","tags":["status:needs-decision","api","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.193713Z","id":"151b3c5d94c881be90bd1ac1f8ba4813be5eeb36c57d88a3c1cafabdb5e39fd4","body":{"detail":"run_opener (tools.rs:2080-2106) and GitCapture::start (git.rs:78) take std::time::Instant::now, which panics on wasm32. Neither runs in a Worker today: a process spawn fails first in run_opener, and a Worker builds ClaxTools without with_git. A Worker's ClaxTools should set Opener::Off so the open tool never tries; gitctx's API takes std's Instant (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2890},"end":{"line":2890},"content_hash":"237e5f5a8a995be40595501dcdb62befa5bb7759b8115cf4144af1f1130bce8d"},"summary":"The open tool's opener and the git capture read std's clock, which panics on wasm32","supersedes":"b85acb3838f6c6555c0086ce2edafdd805797e1b2a2c42ade38cd252687a3db8","tags":["wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:33.450735Z","id":"fa22de6a06cffc033f1d9ad6ee98cca4431c81c9f4d33f60f4039feb7e41c612","body":{"detail":"do_publish fills a missing if_version with a fresh GET of artifact.current_version (tools.rs:1381-1387) and sends that, so the daemon's conflict check (409, tools.rs:1390) can never fire for an agent that leaves if_version out. A version a person, another agent or a page published after this agent's last read is carried over without being merged in. PublishArgs.if_version (tools.rs:93-95) and docs/contract.md:211 document this default, and INSTRUCTIONS (tools.rs:27-28) only asks agents to pass it. The db tools take the opposite stance: a write to an existing document without if_version is refused if_version_required (docs/contract.md:783-784). The CLI copies the same default (crates/clax-commands/src/commands/publish.rs:168-186). Also, when the GET answer lacks current_version the code sends if_version 0 (unwrap_or(0) at tools.rs:1385), which gives a conflict that reads as unrelated to what the agent did.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1378},"end":{"line":1397},"content_hash":"a0df12fc3d99730e29a86db0c2e50d879dd9618c4fec46b846deaefb2de78c99"},"suggested_fix":"Require if_version on an update over MCP, refused like the db tools with a code such as if_version_required that names the current version (the conflict() summary already builds it), and keep the default only for the owner's CLI. If the default stays, have the result say which version it replaced (replaced_version) so a later read can show the agent what it overwrote, and fail with bad_response instead of sending 0 when current_version is missing.","summary":"publish's version check is opt-in: an update without if_version pins whatever is current at that moment, so it silently replaces versions published since the agent last read","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:33.450939Z","id":"247608365a354f833c157a612b394e942bd497436ec841241673fbc3a581e815","body":{"detail":"do_publish_public takes std::time::Instant::now() (tools.rs:1586) and started.elapsed() (tools.rs:1605) after require_session and resolve_id succeed. On wasm32 std's clock is unimplemented and panics; crates/clax-rt/src/lib.rs:33-44 exists to supply web_time's Instant there. The tool set is compiled for the Worker and every tool is listed there (calls.rs test asserts 30 tools), and a Worker MCP client acting in a registered session (DaemonClient::register_session, client.rs:590-609; ClaxTools::in_session) passes require_session. The open thread on tools.rs about run_opener and GitCapture covers those two call sites only, not this one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1586},"end":{"line":1605},"content_hash":"bbbf911a9c61e16235f5ea4bf8a29fb30a22378b316af0241fb0b00a1009a171"},"suggested_fix":"Use clax_rt::time::Instant (web_time on wasm32) for the deadline here, or compute the remaining wait from the daemon's waited_s instead of a local clock. A clippy disallowed-methods entry for std::time::Instant::now in clax-mcp would catch the next one.","summary":"publish_public reads std::time::Instant, which panics on wasm32, so the Worker's tool set panics on a publish_public call that has a session","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","wasm","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:33.451061Z","id":"e7c162dec8b0b38d1f6035700b3bcb88f1012f2046077639e53e54e9b78bfa32","body":{"detail":"wait is clamped to max_ask_wait (50 s under Codex, tools.rs:290-298) so the call ends within Codex's 60 s tool timeout, but the budget covers only ask_wait (tools.rs:1605-1622). Each loop iteration first calls client.push (tools.rs:1589-1593), whose deadline is PUBLISH_TIMEOUT, 120 s (client.rs:34, 1030-1037). When the person approves near the end of the wait, the second push, which now uploads the artifact to the public Clax, starts with no time left in Codex's budget. Codex then abandons the call, and the agent sees a timeout for a publish that may have gone through.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1582},"end":{"line":1627},"content_hash":"dd8f4be80f0ed7828c51052ebcddceb75f317d7d5d322b652452a99f2831e2af"},"suggested_fix":"Bound the whole call by the harness budget: give push a deadline of min(PUBLISH_TIMEOUT, time left), and once the person has answered with no budget left, return {status: 'approval_pending' or 'approved', question_id, call_again: true} so the next call does the push. Alternatively make the post-approval push the daemon's job, so the tool only waits.","summary":"Under Codex, publish_public can outrun Codex's 60 s tool timeout: only the approval wait is bounded by timeout_s, not the pushes around it","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:33.451169Z","id":"6bee6badc6a89c3ab4ee893742aab5be240eac22ff32082fb0a440ba26cf255c","body":{"detail":"Files upload one at a time and the first failure returns through `?` (tools.rs:1683-1687), so the result is an error with no `assets` list. docs/contract.md (asset_upload: 'a failure part way leaves the earlier files uploaded') documents the partial upload but the agent is not told which files succeeded or their URLs. Assets are not deduplicated (crates/clax-store/src/assets.rs add_asset_async mints a new ULID for each upload), so the natural retry of the same file_paths stores the earlier files again. The failures that stop it partway are mostly knowable before any upload: unsupported_type and asset_too_large are checked per file by the daemon (assets.rs:163-174) after the earlier files are stored.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1680},"end":{"line":1696},"content_hash":"7eb4d9cc68b83ac8a852e8893948ad3c0fae8a61621fb4ef8c12d2cbfec2f1e7"},"suggested_fix":"Check every file's inferred content type and size before uploading any (the same rules as clax_store::assets::is_supported and MAX_ASSET_BYTES, moved to clax-core so the tools can share them), and on a failure part way return the error with an extra `uploaded` field listing the assets already stored ({path, id, url}), or return per-file results with an `error` entry each.","summary":"asset_upload loses the URLs of files it already uploaded when a later file fails, and a retry duplicates them","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/target.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:33.451212Z","id":"c04d4a854c01791a69ac417de5231ce9333edb02bf7f86e077a8a5be01d4d488","body":{"detail":"Any http(s) URL whose port equals the daemon base's port is read as an artifact reference, whatever its host (target.rs:43-48). A remote daemon's base is its configured URL (client.rs:1904-1910, remote_endpoint) and a hosted Clax is served on https; with such a base (the fixture covers daemon_base 'https://localhost', plugins/pi/test/fixtures/contract.json), watch, comments_read or ask with a page URL such as https://staging.example.com/ has port 443 == 443, artifact_ref finds no /a/<id> and the tool answers invalid_id \"... is not an artifact ID, a Clax URL, or an http(s) page URL\", which is wrong on its face. A page whose path happens to contain /a/<12-char ID> would instead be taken for an artifact. The rule is shared with the Pi extension through the fixture, so both clients have it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":53},"content_hash":"29fd037fdfef6b8a2064be85b9afd30d33a1bba946c53578bf7a3e82cdcb4311"},"suggested_fix":"Compare host as well as port when the daemon base names a host that is not a loopback or LAN address (keep the any-host rule only for loopback/LAN bases, where it is needed for 127.0.0.1, localhost, <id>.localhost and a LAN address), and add fixture cases for an https daemon base with an https page URL on another host.","summary":"target() tells the daemon's URLs from page URLs by port alone, so with a daemon on https's default port every https page URL is refused invalid_id","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:33.451311Z","id":"50c6b405f9ad7cca63356d5f0ade2ea3445e065d095769a18e975cbe5cf4fc57","body":{"detail":"invoke (tools.rs:2927-2931) turns a parse_json_object failure into CallToolResult::error with the bare message text, and the stdio path does the same: rmcp 3.5.0's tool router converts its 'failed to deserialize parameters:' invalid_params into an error result (rmcp src/handler/server/router/tool.rs:144-156). docs/contract.md:133-138 says such arguments are 'a protocol-level invalid-params error, not a tool result'; the module doc of crates/clax-mcp/src/render.rs:1-3 says every result's first block is a JSON object. So a wrong type, a missing required field or an unknown field (every args struct has deny_unknown_fields) yields isError: true with text such as 'failed to deserialize parameters: unknown field `urll`', with no error.code an agent or crates/clax-commands/src/commands/tools.rs:39-49 (which parses the first block as JSON) can read.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2920},"end":{"line":2936},"content_hash":"036d90c610e379f61c8342a3501f477b9e997c83d7482082724f699214e36b67"},"suggested_fix":"Wrap the deserialization failure as render::error(\"invalid_args\", <message>, {}) in invoke, and in call_tool map the router's plain-text argument error the same way, so every error result has the documented shape; then update docs/contract.md:133-138 and add a test that an unknown field yields error.code invalid_args over both /mcp and stdio.","summary":"Arguments that fail a tool's schema come back as a plain-text error result, while docs/contract.md says they are a protocol-level invalid-params error and every other error is JSON","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:33.451416Z","id":"30e7080fb4b3dd47848f46d5134d9df27324cb484eaa45de95a22da92ea6ca49","body":{"detail":"create and publish_version run under a 120 s deadline (client.rs:34), and a timeout, or a connection dropped mid-request, is not retried because 'the request may have taken effect' (transport_error, client.rs:2178-2204). The tool then answers timeout with 'for a publish, read the artifact before retrying' (render.rs:214-218), but a create has no artifact ID yet to read, so the agent's retry makes a second artifact; an update's retry gets a conflict at best. The daemon already deduplicates publishes by Idempotency-Key for agent-token callers (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:155-223, publish_key/replayed), which is the remote-mode path (attempt_signed), but only clax-server/src/public.rs sends one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":983},"end":{"line":1004},"content_hash":"8ec64210fb68451e0af410144b9b216055074c57ffc736faf22ad5fde2adbb5d"},"suggested_fix":"Send an Idempotency-Key on create and publish_version, derived from the call ID (CallScope::header().call_id), and return it in the timeout error as `idempotency_key` with a tool argument to resend it on retry; or make the timeout message for a create say to `list` (newest first) before retrying. Extending publish_key to local sessions would cover the stdio shim too.","summary":"A create or publish that times out cannot be retried safely: the MCP client sends no Idempotency-Key, and a timed-out create leaves the agent no ID to read","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:01.492446Z","id":"1525f4fe245fef0074919c63965bed154ae90602f63deeb4f2d315c6c7198b94","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs:983-1004: create and publish_version build POST requests with .timeout(PUBLISH_TIMEOUT) (120 s, client.rs:34) and no idempotency header; `grep -rn -i idempotency crates/clax-mcp/src` matches only the .qual file. transport_error (client.rs:2178-2204) marks a timeout refreshable: false. render.rs:214-218 answers ClientError::Timeout with 'for a publish, read the artifact before retrying', which a create has no ID for. The daemon side exists: crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:155-223 (IDEMPOTENCY_HEADER, publish_key, replayed) dedups keyed publishes from agent-token grants; the only sender is crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:209/360.","kind":"comment","references":"30e7080fb4b3dd47848f46d5134d9df27324cb484eaa45de95a22da92ea6ca49","summary":"confirmed: create and publish_version send no Idempotency-Key, and a timeout is not retried","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/target.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:01.492983Z","id":"1d2d381d8240c089c593892ef58cae6a5126fd41416e192467498a067c3772b4","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-mcp/src/target.rs:42-48: the URL is a Page only when daemon_port is None or u.port_or_known_default() != daemon_port; the host is never compared. With daemon_base https://<host> (port 443), https://staging.example.com/ has port 443, so it falls to artifact_ref and fails with invalid_id (target.rs:18-24). The base passed is self.browser_base() (tools.rs:1203), which for a remote daemon is remote.config.url (client.rs:1904-1910). plugins/pi/test/fixtures/contract.json:181-185 has a case with daemon_base https://localhost, so the shared fixture accepts an https base.","kind":"comment","references":"c04d4a854c01791a69ac417de5231ce9333edb02bf7f86e077a8a5be01d4d488","summary":"confirmed: target() compares only ports, so an https daemon base makes every https page URL an artifact reference","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:01.493403Z","id":"064451c140551336b5f4a9ee3b5d235f53ce3db82c92d8f33f1767e7717385cd","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:1380-1387: `None => { let got = self.client.get(&id)...; got[\"artifact\"][\"current_version\"].as_u64().unwrap_or(0) as u32 }` then body[\"if_version\"] = current. PublishArgs.if_version doc (tools.rs:93-95) and docs/contract.md:211 state the default; docs/contract.md:783-784 shows db writes refuse if_version_required instead. crates/clax-commands/src/commands/publish.rs:168-175 has the same default (there with .context(...) rather than unwrap_or(0)).","kind":"comment","references":"fa22de6a06cffc033f1d9ad6ee98cca4431c81c9f4d33f60f4039feb7e41c612","summary":"confirmed: an update without if_version fetches and sends the current version, so it never conflicts; a missing current_version sends 0","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:01.493809Z","id":"32bb96d320c9b495e435d0a3903d8cd299eaba20cd61f5f788d2831adff6721d","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:1582-1585 clamps wait to max_ask_wait (50 under codex, tools.rs:290-298); started is taken at 1586 and consulted only for `left` before ask_wait (1605-1622). The loop's first statement, self.client.push(&id, &body) (1589-1593), is not bounded by `left`; push uses .timeout(PUBLISH_TIMEOUT) (client.rs:1027-1035, 120 s at client.rs:34). After an approval that arrives near the end of the wait, the loop pushes again with no remaining budget.","kind":"comment","references":"e7c162dec8b0b38d1f6035700b3bcb88f1012f2046077639e53e54e9b78bfa32","summary":"confirmed: only ask_wait is bounded by the Codex-clamped wait; each push runs under the 120 s PUBLISH_TIMEOUT","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:01.494218Z","id":"47c069aec9a2f367ea47b1a009562ebb2dbd3c5787afa260d59aa206dd41a2ce","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:1586 `let started = std::time::Instant::now();` runs after require_session (1580) and resolve_id (1581), before any push. crates/clax-rt/src/lib.rs:32-44 documents that std::time::Instant::now panics on wasm32 and re-exports web_time as clax_rt::wall. The tool set is served on wasm32: crates/clax-server/src/routes/mcp_http.rs:121-135 has a cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\") Shared = Arc<SendWrapper<ClaxTools>>, and its module doc (mcp_http.rs:20-38) says an agent token's initialize registers a session, so require_session passes. clax-worker's Cargo.lock lists clax-mcp as a dependency.","kind":"comment","references":"247608365a354f833c157a612b394e942bd497436ec841241673fbc3a581e815","summary":"confirmed: do_publish_public calls std::time::Instant::now, which panics on wasm32, in code the Worker's /mcp serves","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:01.494631Z","id":"1854af828baf10b617fa90db094f8a2fe702fa21f485789c90c8d95eb8c5c1b7","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:1680-1696: each upload_asset result goes through .map_err(|e| self.fail(e))?, so an error returns before `Ok(json!({\"assets\": assets}))` and the collected `assets` are discarded. docs/contract.md:546-548 says 'a failure part way leaves the earlier files uploaded'. crates/clax-store/src/assets.rs:155-180: add_asset_async checks is_supported and MAX_ASSET_BYTES per file and mints id: new_ulid() for each upload, with no lookup by content hash, so a retry stores the earlier files again.","kind":"comment","references":"6bee6badc6a89c3ab4ee893742aab5be240eac22ff32082fb0a440ba26cf255c","summary":"confirmed: a part-way upload failure returns only the error, dropping the assets already stored, and uploads are not deduplicated","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:01.495179Z","id":"4b53855370fbbbeda97f1312818eafaca3dc3a3ccd8166222a9ef1f950e45df5","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:2926-2931: a parse_json_object error becomes CallToolResult::error(vec![ContentBlock::text(e.message)]). rmcp 3.5.0 src/handler/server/router/tool.rs:146-156 (into_tool_argument_error) turns 'failed to deserialize parameters:' invalid_params into the same plain-text error result on the router path. docs/contract.md:133-137 says such arguments are 'a protocol-level invalid-params error, not a tool result'; crates/clax-mcp/src/render.rs:1-3 says every result's first text block is a JSON object; crates/clax-commands/src/commands/tools.rs:46 parses that first block with serde_json::from_str, which fails on this text.","kind":"comment","references":"50c6b405f9ad7cca63356d5f0ade2ea3445e065d095769a18e975cbe5cf4fc57","summary":"confirmed: schema failures come back as a plain-text error result, contradicting docs/contract.md and render.rs's JSON-first-block rule","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:19:43.040612Z","id":"f30f20e36d7429d6c39a039719134182312036899fe1023e63a293649a7f19ef","body":{"detail":"Comment and reply bodies render as Markdown in the shell and the extension (docs/contract.md, Comments and feedback), so an agent may format replies with lists, code blocks and links. The description, plugins/pi/test/fixtures/contract.json and the skills' generated tool blocks change together (scripts/sync-skill-tools.py --check).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":3160},"end":{"line":3160},"content_hash":"dd757b08ef0bbdca3577c3bf58ffbb38875df5b774e71513fbfc1f5de44d58fb"},"summary":"comments_reply's description does not say that replies render as Markdown","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:59:42.573283Z","id":"8dfe694663402629fa8ef30adb611b885ab9eeced99a3cb569c03224e224bbf9","body":{"detail":"Done (66370dbc6, test an_update_without_a_known_current_version_is_bad_response in crates/clax-mcp/tests/tools.rs; Pi mirrors it in plugins/pi/src/clax.ts): an update without if_version whose GET lacks artifact.current_version is refused bad_response and nothing is published. Left open, because it changes the agent-facing contract (docs/contract.md publish table: 'Defaults to the artifact's current version'; PublishArgs.if_version doc in crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs; INSTRUCTIONS; the clax skills under plugins/*/skills; Pi's clax_publish): (A) require if_version on an update over MCP, refused like the db tools (docs/contract.md: if_version_required) with the current version named, keeping the default only in `clax publish`, which now computes its own default and passes it to the tool (crates/clax-commands/src/commands/publish.rs); agents that omit it today get a refusal they can recover from in one read. (B) keep the default and add `replaced_version` to the result, so an agent can see what it overwrote, without preventing it. (C) keep the default as documented. Recommendation: A, since an agent that skips the read silently drops a person's or another agent's version, and the db tools already take this stance.","kind":"comment","references":"fa22de6a06cffc033f1d9ad6ee98cca4431c81c9f4d33f60f4039feb7e41c612","summary":"Partly fixed in 66370dbc6: a missing current_version is bad_response, not if_version 0. Whether an MCP update must pass if_version is the owner's call","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:59:42.573731Z","id":"c570ee49ca3ac7af76632a9b2cb39dedd43bb5c05362ac2e9e2d4efdbb4f15eb","body":{"detail":"Follows 30e7080f. Since 66370dbc6 a create's timeout tells the agent to call list and look for the artifact by title before publishing again (CREATE_TIMEOUT in crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs), so it no longer points at an artifact it cannot name. Still open: create and publish_version (crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs:997-1016) send no Idempotency-Key, and crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs publish_key ignores one from the daemon token, so the stdio shim's publishes cannot be deduplicated at all. A key from the call ID alone would not help an agent's retry (a new tool call has a new ID); it needs a tool argument carrying the key across calls (a contract change), and keys for local daemon-token publishes in the store, which today keys them by grant. A title match after list can also find the wrong artifact when titles repeat.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":997},"end":{"line":1016},"content_hash":"ea911f0e83d3eea7a108ec300806ad84890e855c135a2d19441395b2957463b2"},"summary":"A publish that times out still cannot be retried idempotently: no Idempotency-Key is sent, and the daemon honours one only from agent-token grants","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:59:42.574117Z","id":"791da7d647df7b1b76b93bbb132b499ea1bea419aea2ba0799a99b587c8145e4","body":{"detail":"Follows e7c162de. Since eb36834e2 the push after an answer starts only while the wait (at most 50 s under Codex) has time left, else the call returns status answered with call_again. The push itself (client.push, PUBLISH_TIMEOUT in crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs) is not cut to the time left: crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs approval() spends the approval (use_push_approval) before pushing, so a client that gave up mid-push would leave a spent approval and an unknown outcome, and the retry would get approval_used. A push that takes more than about ten seconds after a late answer can therefore still pass Codex's 60 s timeout. Bounding it safely needs the daemon to push after approval on its own, or an approval that is spent only once the push lands.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1626},"end":{"line":1631},"content_hash":"119d8c55bd14641f9f48521628831239b607ad8b395a33f674865de9bfbf6986"},"summary":"publish_public's pushes are still bounded only by the 120 s publish deadline, not by the wait: a slow post-approval push can outrun Codex's tool timeout","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/target.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:53:04.624390Z","id":"9a7ecbe023fef5e4d3193dad31556e5fb0c51f0e38e0716dd106afb28fc2648b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a514f523b","summary":"Fixed (07e2f445c, a514f523b): a daemon on a non-local name owns only its own host and subdomains; a local daemon keeps the port-only rule. a_daemon_on_a_public_name_owns_only_its_own_host, a_daemon_on_a_local_name_owns_every_host_on_its_port and target_matches_the_fixture (Rust and Pi, incl. CGNAT, .ts.net, .home.arpa) pass.","supersedes":"c04d4a854c01791a69ac417de5231ce9333edb02bf7f86e077a8a5be01d4d488","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:53:06.794665Z","id":"f52a18d0ddbf9fe78cdb6a3c188f1a8f04dabbc18154369ea43139b9b551f472","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:81773e6bb","summary":"Fixed: invoke answers deserialize failures as invalid_args JSON and stdio call_tool goes through invoke; calls.rs::arguments_that_fail_the_schema_are_invalid_args passes over MCP and call_direct.","supersedes":"50c6b405f9ad7cca63356d5f0ade2ea3445e065d095769a18e975cbe5cf4fc57","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:53:09.153745Z","id":"3b53e465e4618871cae8aa2e4b882bc42e73b3a79577d81e25f79e2322a974ec","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e8229a332","summary":"Fixed: publish_public measures its wait on ClaxTools' injectable clock (chrono Utc::now, wasm-safe) instead of std::time::Instant; publish_public.rs::an_answer_after_the_wait_ran_out_leaves_the_push_to_the_next_call passes.","supersedes":"247608365a354f833c157a612b394e942bd497436ec841241673fbc3a581e815","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:53:11.700983Z","id":"e801290e409d54e7fe0ebeef7cd47e8798b2fc8c3097ce4ca4649eaab2885954","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:1315b7161","summary":"Fixed: every file is checked before any upload, and a part-way failure returns path and uploaded; asset_upload_refuses_an_unsupported_file_before_uploading_any and asset_upload_failing_part_way_names_the_assets_already_uploaded pass (Pi twin tested in eb0be31ab).","supersedes":"6bee6badc6a89c3ab4ee893742aab5be240eac22ff32082fb0a440ba26cf255c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:53:15.222478Z","id":"ddd5e9dfbbaf88eceabc38c7986653090b25cc15640ab1b9ccecb19d3ef71812","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"30e7080fb4b3dd47848f46d5134d9df27324cb484eaa45de95a22da92ea6ca49","summary":"Partly fixed in 56f8e55a1: a create's timeout now tells the agent to call list and look for the artifact by title before publishing again (test a_create_that_times_out_says_to_look_for_the_artifact_with_list). A real Idempotency-Key is deferred to concern c570ee49 on crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs.","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:53:15.223660Z","id":"b76e10fe01a311e490785812489f69f11b772ecafd9dc6588d242497d55d34c7","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e7c162dec8b0b38d1f6035700b3bcb88f1012f2046077639e53e54e9b78bfa32","summary":"Partly fixed in e8229a332: the push after an answer starts only while the wait has time left, otherwise the call returns status answered with call_again. Bounding the push itself is deferred to concern 791da7d6 on crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs.","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:53:15.224924Z","id":"04fd8cb742db36263c8ae4d60f28eee8f1902a9d4c140983bfcc33148c1f0118","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"fa22de6a06cffc033f1d9ad6ee98cca4431c81c9f4d33f60f4039feb7e41c612","summary":"Partly fixed in 56f8e55a1: an update whose current_version is unknown is now bad_response instead of if_version 0 (test an_update_without_a_known_current_version_is_bad_response). Whether to require if_version waits on the owner (reply 8dfe6946).","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:04:26.750431Z","id":"fb2c9613376f76367c3f10f3cdc463ec11337ddaac6284c569eb37ebd9a0d3e3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8e7b1ea2f","summary":"comments_reply's description and its text field now say a reply renders as GitHub-flavoured Markdown with no images and no raw HTML (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs, plugins/pi/src/clax.ts, plugins/pi/test/fixtures/contract.json, the four skills' tool references, docs/contract.md). bazelisk test //crates/clax-mcp/... //plugins/pi:test //plugins/pi:typecheck: 5 of 5 pass; scripts/sync-skill-tools.py --check exits 0.","supersedes":"f30f20e36d7429d6c39a039719134182312036899fe1023e63a293649a7f19ef","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:35:40.461924Z","id":"ca5598fb788823edf79d648e1be8c3281f9f5de3096c9fcf40660cb4e7d53ede","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the tool set is one list for every agent (plugins/pi/test/fixtures/contract.json, the skills' generated tool blocks, ClaxTools::tool_count), with no per-caller tools. Owner-only tools would show to every person's agent and answer 403 owner_only to most of them. Tag management stays with the owner's browser (the UI phase) and the CLI (clax tags create|edit|delete, crates/clax-commands/src/commands/tags.rs); POST/PATCH/DELETE /api/tags already admit the owner's agents for scripts.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":3323},"end":{"line":3345},"content_hash":"7be5e759caa41ef66947d63dd436b2acf43c7567ecc2d846e5a9c77ca28c319a"},"summary":"Owner-only MCP tools to make, rename, recolour and delete tags","tags":["revisit:the tool scheme lists tools per caller, or owners ask to manage tags from an agent","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:35:40.462189Z","id":"84a77ce3934bb65027436fc58fe4606d242cfbb38f031d43aa86b5ea5207e308","body":{"detail":"Not taken: PublishRequest (crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs) is shared with the public-twin pushes and the store's create path; adding tags there spreads an owner-managed list into every publish path. The tools check the names first (check_tags, an unknown tag publishes nothing) and add them after with PATCH /api/artifacts/<id>/tags. Accepted risk: a version can land without its tags when that PATCH is refused (admin_only for an editor's publish) or fails; the result reports it as tags_error and the CLI's publish then exits non-zero after printing the version.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1423},"end":{"line":1426},"content_hash":"94d9cf17d34b42e5cf7ebe720bd5fbb2937e166c42d359cdef110c22431edd3e"},"summary":"Apply publish's tags in the publish request itself, atomically with the version","tags":["revisit:a publish that lands without its tags confuses people or agents in practice","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:53:17.993009Z","id":"ca4151ca402cf228bf287424d07cfe394c8526e41dc3609e40fbb8fe6db8ef16","body":{"detail":"The publish-then-PATCH design (alternative 84a77ce3) rests on a refused PATCH being reported as tags_error beside the version, and crates/clax-commands/src/commands/publish.rs then bails after printing. grep -rn tags_error over crates/*/tests, crates/clax-mcp/src and plugins/pi/test finds only this code: no test publishes a new version of another's artifact as an editor with tags and checks that the version lands, tags_error carries admin_only, and the CLI exits non-zero.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1480},"end":{"line":1490},"content_hash":"3451e814249cfaef7a0fcaeb4d8cc0ca43ba54fa22de5e68fd5afe274c411d1b"},"suggested_fix":"Add one MCP test (an editor's agent publishing to the owner's artifact with tags), one Pi test with the same fixture, and a CLI test asserting the exit status and the printed version.","summary":"No test covers publish's tags_error path in the MCP tool, the Pi mirror or the CLI's non-zero exit","tags":["review","review:artifact-tags","tests","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:55:11.178755Z","id":"a0040dcca97a3a5d4d0499ff80ac06d9a55d8996190e6a75e57b98b4d443914c","body":{"detail":"grep -rn tags_error crates/ plugins/pi (node_modules excluded) returns only crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:1487-1488, crates/clax-commands/src/commands/publish.rs:218 and :244, plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1137, and .qual records; no hit under crates/*/tests, plugins/pi/test, or any #[cfg(test)] module.","kind":"comment","references":"ca4151ca402cf228bf287424d07cfe394c8526e41dc3609e40fbb8fe6db8ef16","summary":"confirmed: no test exercises tags_error in the MCP tool, the Pi mirror or the CLI exit","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:14:34.711379Z","id":"e27452ece7632244ee481cd7ff18671aa7f0a5fe6e81e267f5f3f9c0072b3df3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:37446d96b","summary":"Fixed in 37446d96b: tools::a_publish_whose_tags_are_refused_lands_and_reports_tags_error (MCP), the Pi test 'publishes a version whose tags are refused and reports tags_error beside it', and cli::a_publish_whose_tags_are_refused_publishes_and_exits_non_zero each publish past the 20-tag bound and check the version lands, tags_error carries too_many_tags, and the CLI exits non-zero (bazelisk test //crates/clax-mcp:all //crates/clax-cli:all //plugins/pi:test PASSED)","supersedes":"ca4151ca402cf228bf287424d07cfe394c8526e41dc3609e40fbb8fe6db8ef16","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:10:59.097814Z","id":"28c463ad3c42b96db882f3b4d32544169a420d456d9635fba83a04681e0578e0","body":{"detail":"Follows e7c162de. Since eb36834e2 the push after an answer starts only while the wait (at most 50 s under Codex) has time left, else the call returns status answered with call_again. The push itself (client.push, PUBLISH_TIMEOUT in crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs) is not cut to the time left: crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs approval() spends the approval (use_push_approval) before pushing, so a client that gave up mid-push would leave a spent approval and an unknown outcome, and the retry would get approval_used. A push that takes more than about ten seconds after a late answer can therefore still pass Codex's 60 s timeout. Bounding it safely needs the daemon to push after approval on its own, or an approval that is spent only once the push lands.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1751},"end":{"line":1756},"content_hash":"119d8c55bd14641f9f48521628831239b607ad8b395a33f674865de9bfbf6986"},"summary":"publish_public's pushes are still bounded only by the 120 s publish deadline, not by the wait: a slow post-approval push can outrun Codex's tool timeout","supersedes":"791da7d647df7b1b76b93bbb132b499ea1bea419aea2ba0799a99b587c8145e4","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:39:50.649542Z","id":"0ab48c282afebc330ca9411ae758556febdf4acb809018355c50f48f0b29a4f9","body":{"detail":"publish_public already asks the person and waits (question_id, timeout_s, call_again), so site_access reuses its shape and the tool list stays as plugins/pi/test/fixtures/contract.json and the skills give it; plugins/pi/src/clax.ts mirrors it. A tool of its own (say open_site {url_or_id, open}) would read more plainly and would work on a hosted Clax's /mcp, which has no session for publish_public's question.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":204},"end":{"line":208},"content_hash":"1ca69d9ee207cedc5b364bae2a749a41a68d5c3b6e4388b00657e90e69a51305"},"summary":"Opening a site to the world as a tool of its own rather than publish_public's site_access","tags":["status:needs-decision","revisit:agents misuse publish_public's site_access or a hosted /mcp agent needs to open a site","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:41:55.308215Z","id":"daf502c496379ac77c25e48544e1ccacc81d43735cafd8c8a388893076776156","body":{"detail":"do_publish fills a missing if_version with a fresh GET of artifact.current_version (tools.rs:1381-1387) and sends that, so the daemon's conflict check (409, tools.rs:1390) can never fire for an agent that leaves if_version out. A version a person, another agent or a page published after this agent's last read is carried over without being merged in. PublishArgs.if_version (tools.rs:93-95) and docs/contract.md:211 document this default, and INSTRUCTIONS (tools.rs:27-28) only asks agents to pass it. The db tools take the opposite stance: a write to an existing document without if_version is refused if_version_required (docs/contract.md:783-784). The CLI copies the same default (crates/clax-commands/src/commands/publish.rs:168-186). Also, when the GET answer lacks current_version the code sends if_version 0 (unwrap_or(0) at tools.rs:1385), which gives a conflict that reads as unrelated to what the agent did.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1383},"end":{"line":1402},"content_hash":"ad71e3a36f493fd65ec674359827ee3312a15d4df65bc9cb206b1f05ccd10d04"},"suggested_fix":"Require if_version on an update over MCP, refused like the db tools with a code such as if_version_required that names the current version (the conflict() summary already builds it), and keep the default only for the owner's CLI. If the default stays, have the result say which version it replaced (replaced_version) so a later read can show the agent what it overwrote, and fail with bad_response instead of sending 0 when current_version is missing.","summary":"publish's version check is opt-in: an update without if_version pins whatever is current at that moment, so it silently replaces versions published since the agent last read","supersedes":"fa22de6a06cffc033f1d9ad6ee98cca4431c81c9f4d33f60f4039feb7e41c612","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:41:55.326820Z","id":"37aa66a2bfd0d339d2e5db5916907856516539254f1d28ff5ace536e1e3efd81","body":{"detail":"Not taken: PublishRequest (crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs) is shared with the public-twin pushes and the store's create path; adding tags there spreads an owner-managed list into every publish path. The tools check the names first (check_tags, an unknown tag publishes nothing) and add them after with PATCH /api/artifacts/<id>/tags. Accepted risk: a version can land without its tags when that PATCH is refused (admin_only for an editor's publish) or fails; the result reports it as tags_error and the CLI's publish then exits non-zero after printing the version.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1428},"end":{"line":1431},"content_hash":"5e30f7e902d0cfa0a8ad3290f44b29af0a89384d72828874bfa5dc44e0d7977b"},"summary":"Apply publish's tags in the publish request itself, atomically with the version","supersedes":"84a77ce3934bb65027436fc58fe4606d242cfbb38f031d43aa86b5ea5207e308","tags":["revisit:a publish that lands without its tags confuses people or agents in practice","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:41:55.345377Z","id":"05a9df444baba5ba2fcfc7991c0ffa428593d56da9b9d0deefdf5380b48564e3","body":{"detail":"wait is clamped to max_ask_wait (50 s under Codex, tools.rs:290-298) so the call ends within Codex's 60 s tool timeout, but the budget covers only ask_wait (tools.rs:1605-1622). Each loop iteration first calls client.push (tools.rs:1589-1593), whose deadline is PUBLISH_TIMEOUT, 120 s (client.rs:34, 1030-1037). When the person approves near the end of the wait, the second push, which now uploads the artifact to the public Clax, starts with no time left in Codex's budget. Codex then abandons the call, and the agent sees a timeout for a publish that may have gone through.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1587},"end":{"line":1632},"content_hash":"17de9000141cd492c5c2e4b620a713a24dc82eb22fb7f598e9893d9806cfa942"},"suggested_fix":"Bound the whole call by the harness budget: give push a deadline of min(PUBLISH_TIMEOUT, time left), and once the person has answered with no budget left, return {status: 'approval_pending' or 'approved', question_id, call_again: true} so the next call does the push. Alternatively make the post-approval push the daemon's job, so the tool only waits.","summary":"Under Codex, publish_public can outrun Codex's 60 s tool timeout: only the approval wait is bounded by timeout_s, not the pushes around it","supersedes":"e7c162dec8b0b38d1f6035700b3bcb88f1012f2046077639e53e54e9b78bfa32","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:41:55.364196Z","id":"068a786787041c86e9b96db9bed558bad592b3b1c922d1e7840e385201916f7b","body":{"detail":"Follows e7c162de. Since eb36834e2 the push after an answer starts only while the wait (at most 50 s under Codex) has time left, else the call returns status answered with call_again. The push itself (client.push, PUBLISH_TIMEOUT in crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs) is not cut to the time left: crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs approval() spends the approval (use_push_approval) before pushing, so a client that gave up mid-push would leave a spent approval and an unknown outcome, and the retry would get approval_used. A push that takes more than about ten seconds after a late answer can therefore still pass Codex's 60 s timeout. Bounding it safely needs the daemon to push after approval on its own, or an approval that is spent only once the push lands.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1756},"end":{"line":1761},"content_hash":"f76fc2dd83677180f604564dfc48e0aad425d5cbfbb097a3a9d6246af239ed3b"},"summary":"publish_public's pushes are still bounded only by the 120 s publish deadline, not by the wait: a slow post-approval push can outrun Codex's tool timeout","supersedes":"28c463ad3c42b96db882f3b4d32544169a420d456d9635fba83a04681e0578e0","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:41:55.382731Z","id":"d70dc2e21592bb4c042ec42eafdc19f8f41ba8284c34716a802eca8197fbbdc9","body":{"detail":"The token is handed to the session (its holder, whose pushes are its person's), so the tool calls POST /api/sessions/<sid>/git-token/<id>. Over /mcp and /mcp/json (crates/clax-server/tests/api_mcp.rs mcp_git_remote_without_a_session_is_no_session) there is no session; an agent reaches the Worker's git remotes only through the stdio shim's registered session, as draft does.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2361},"end":{"line":2384},"content_hash":"7cb939860bb03c538461b3cf3ceb13ee90bbf7af16446f93bc92370903596379"},"summary":"git_remote needs a harness session, so it answers no_session over the /mcp endpoints, which have none","supersedes":"485d9c6573ae4b205cda0f967f5a2e207a6e22cecce1f241ec602b3b5566d7a4","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:41:55.401178Z","id":"ac7841e8dceff6e572119870019027938f57753e139da01a27deda0a272254f0","body":{"detail":"do_ask creates the question and then waits in ask_wait for up to timeout_s (default 600 s; 50 s under Codex). tell_terminal (\"Asked in Clax: <url>\") is set only while the result's status is open, so it reaches the agent only after the wait runs out, never when the person answers within it; meanwhile the terminal shows the pending tool call (plugins/pi/src/clax.ts ask behaves the same). The skills' \"## Where to ask\" step 3 and INSTRUCTIONS say this as it is. Options: (a) the create returns at once with tell_terminal and call_again: true, and the agent writes the line and calls again with question_id; it works the same in all four harnesses; (b) the agent writes \"Asked in Clax: <place>\" in chat before calling ask (it knows the artifact and thread, not the browser base URL); (c) send the line as an MCP progress or log notification at create time, in harnesses that show those.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2394},"end":{"line":2501},"content_hash":"c74b24ef0d6d44c95a71c0194762f039bac1ec6f7f23c1d08685ce4fe532bf03"},"summary":"Tell the terminal where a Clax question waits while ask is still waiting, rather than only in the result's tell_terminal after the wait","supersedes":"73a0dec97bc00ceba6cae9e7c7909ac91001902b109a50ffffa6375bd38514b1","tags":["revisit:the owner picks (a), (b) or (c), or people report not knowing where a question waits","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:41:55.419642Z","id":"b4e0c98a1ecb8ec55f0b839af8882f28e82846edd5550796c2019850ec328c69","body":{"detail":"An ask with in_terminal: true takes the full question shape and validates it like any ask (clax_core::questions::validate_ask): options and all are stored and shown on the terminal card. Design spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md section 3 has the agent post only the headers; the tools do not enforce that, so a card may show options the person answers in the terminal.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2426},"end":{"line":2435},"content_hash":"14043b6245c523bdc2dcc10d81919604d1db8ec56225c508a38c17485a7ee7f0"},"summary":"Limit an in-terminal ask to the questions' headers","supersedes":"ffe18e7b92c41ac8d7e6dece94385f627555ed7889f317e3ded8765cd1882124","tags":["revisit:terminal cards show options that read as answerable in Clax","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:41:55.437976Z","id":"1baa963c74a9932fcd4f1e4d6a368c04e91aa4d833031ff3506c6ada7825d5b1","body":{"detail":"ask's cancel results (do_ask's cancel arm, here; plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1594-1603) pass no suggestion to ask_result, and approval results (approval_result, crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs:2473; plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1663) carry none. A cancel ends a question the agent is done with and an approval asks to see withheld content: neither answers where to ask the person next, and the feedback poll and question create and poll already carry the suggestion. Adding it would cost one GET /api/sessions/{id}/where-to-ask per call.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2465},"end":{"line":2482},"content_hash":"2f9928284b2929e0fb9978e566a7facaf2f0e1a234948a644c92e819566a06c2"},"summary":"Carry where_to_ask on ask's cancel and approval results too","supersedes":"2c48e2a8efea3e5aed5bbc3bf4993d93a75a35514ba59b3b2b3b993dedc25c48","tags":["revisit:an agent cancels an in-terminal question and then asks again without a fresh suggestion","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:41:55.456558Z","id":"fdcfc468e8fa9f3e71223a7e58d314cd29ba8ab2fd2b3bc33885d1653f4f7139","body":{"detail":"ask_result sets surface_open (whether a Clax surface of the person was open when the question was created, remembered in ask_surface) on every open question asked in Clax; Pi's tool does the same (plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1726), and docs/contract.md:2857 describes it. Its only use for agents was the skills' 'If it also says surface_open: false, the person may not have Clax open' fallback to asking in chat too (plugins/*/skills/clax/SKILL.md at aa0696af3), which the skills dropped when they gained '## Where to ask': an agent asks on one surface and never mirrors the question in chat. The where_to_ask suggestion now tells the agent whether Clax can show a question. Question for the owner: drop surface_open from the ask result (and ask_surface with it), or keep it and document it as informational.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2653},"end":{"line":2658},"content_hash":"26de2b32d812db42676923adb70dbb5b7eeaff3812359e465f241b2a8c257716"},"summary":"The ask result still carries surface_open for an open Clax question, but no agent instruction explains it any more","supersedes":"ebf6dec5dc65a023edd7461b703f3e39c62ef4390ac6a2bd572e722d904cdbf0","tags":["status:needs-decision","api","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:41:55.475818Z","id":"ea8490f0aefdd1e86f99cdc3b411e5e1c94bcd4ef53f3d8150cf6c861411d3fa","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the tool set is one list for every agent (plugins/pi/test/fixtures/contract.json, the skills' generated tool blocks, ClaxTools::tool_count), with no per-caller tools. Owner-only tools would show to every person's agent and answer 403 owner_only to most of them. Tag management stays with the owner's browser (the UI phase) and the CLI (clax tags create|edit|delete, crates/clax-commands/src/commands/tags.rs); POST/PATCH/DELETE /api/tags already admit the owner's agents for scripts.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":3394},"end":{"line":3416},"content_hash":"73ad64a8031b3702ae7405642b45e89e67c00b942c1a8eeae57abea87de358d1"},"summary":"Owner-only MCP tools to make, rename, recolour and delete tags","supersedes":"ca5598fb788823edf79d648e1be8c3281f9f5de3096c9fcf40660cb4e7d53ede","tags":["revisit:the tool scheme lists tools per caller, or owners ask to manage tags from an agent","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:07.828605Z","id":"febc701e18446b8b1e31099d812251c08a8668f049bc81977f71736c61e91af3","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the tool set is one list for every agent (plugins/pi/test/fixtures/contract.json, the skills' generated tool blocks, ClaxTools::tool_count), with no per-caller tools. Owner-only tools would show to every person's agent and answer 403 owner_only to most of them. Tag management stays with the owner's browser (the UI phase) and the CLI (clax tags create|edit|delete, crates/clax-commands/src/commands/tags.rs); POST/PATCH/DELETE /api/tags already admit the owner's agents for scripts.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":3328},"end":{"line":3350},"content_hash":"7be5e759caa41ef66947d63dd436b2acf43c7567ecc2d846e5a9c77ca28c319a"},"summary":"Owner-only MCP tools to make, rename, recolour and delete tags","supersedes":"ca5598fb788823edf79d648e1be8c3281f9f5de3096c9fcf40660cb4e7d53ede","tags":["revisit:the tool scheme lists tools per caller, or owners ask to manage tags from an agent","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:38:53.538921Z","id":"7cca37c57a18dcdc9af8bf5df0bf6dbaf66202a424f51734c55c20a1a0e18c4d","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the tool set is one list for every agent (plugins/pi/test/fixtures/contract.json, the skills' generated tool blocks, ClaxTools::tool_count), with no per-caller tools. Owner-only tools would show to every person's agent and answer 403 owner_only to most of them. Tag management stays with the owner's browser (the UI phase) and the CLI (clax tags create|edit|delete, crates/clax-commands/src/commands/tags.rs); POST/PATCH/DELETE /api/tags already admit the owner's agents for scripts.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":3399},"end":{"line":3421},"content_hash":"73ad64a8031b3702ae7405642b45e89e67c00b942c1a8eeae57abea87de358d1"},"summary":"Owner-only MCP tools to make, rename, recolour and delete tags","supersedes":"ea8490f0aefdd1e86f99cdc3b411e5e1c94bcd4ef53f3d8150cf6c861411d3fa","tags":["revisit:the tool scheme lists tools per caller, or owners ask to manage tags from an agent","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:38:54.771866Z","id":"d6e416b070ea0deded6296cf47e6eb7cc55c65268b3b33c043522e3a9a18ec04","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the tool set is one list for every agent (plugins/pi/test/fixtures/contract.json, the skills' generated tool blocks, ClaxTools::tool_count), with no per-caller tools. Owner-only tools would show to every person's agent and answer 403 owner_only to most of them. Tag management stays with the owner's browser (the UI phase) and the CLI (clax tags create|edit|delete, crates/clax-commands/src/commands/tags.rs); POST/PATCH/DELETE /api/tags already admit the owner's agents for scripts.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":3333},"end":{"line":3355},"content_hash":"16c9e8bd5f8c1cf9dd5c2dab5798d0ee6046c8bb51357928aa0536325dab9184"},"summary":"Owner-only MCP tools to make, rename, recolour and delete tags","supersedes":"febc701e18446b8b1e31099d812251c08a8668f049bc81977f71736c61e91af3","tags":["revisit:the tool scheme lists tools per caller, or owners ask to manage tags from an agent","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T00:00:56.709714Z","id":"cca4d2885d22f62b9bec2fb83db7992f792efb18ebb9d0244917d4725a2cd1d8","body":{"detail":"opener_target hands open (macOS) or xdg-open a path under <home>/login/ so that a login code never appears on a command line (clax_core::login_page). The platform opener opens that path with the default application for .html files. On a machine where that is an editor, clax open and the MCP and Pi open tools open the page there, the code is not redeemed, and the browser stays cold until clax login's link is pasted. plugins/pi/src/clax.ts openSignedIn does the same.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3348},"end":{"line":3356},"content_hash":"84b6954a7ad7b4bfd30a70b41052f19b0b613719c8e94deb9373311a67a6ac98"},"summary":"The opener is given a .html file path, which opens in the app the system pairs with HTML files, not necessarily the browser","tags":["local-trust","follow-up","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T00:57:07.236133Z","id":"d9b8b2aa79223cc048a230165d1e2edcd55663bbc3ef3c556fff564cd9cfe619","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:1e3fda107","summary":"The opener is no longer given a .html path: 1e3fda107 removed the login page (clax_core::login_page), and on macOS opens the URL by osascript's open location (open_location_script in crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs), which goes to the default browser for http. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-mcp/... passes, including open_status::open_hands_the_opener_a_login_link_the_platforms_way (the opener reads 'open location \"http://localhost:<port>/login?code=cxi_…\"' on stdin with no argument) and tools::tests::only_a_plain_http_url_becomes_an_open_location_script.","supersedes":"cca4d2885d22f62b9bec2fb83db7992f792efb18ebb9d0244917d4725a2cd1d8","tags":["session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T01:47:02.020450Z","id":"9cfcc851196eb6cdb4f235d55fca33babd317a2f76d66c68d4c9dcbcbd13ad52","body":{"detail":"ClaxTools::target falls back to Target::Page on any error of resolve_url, so a daemon from before the route (404), or one that fails it, keeps today's page behaviour; a daemon that cannot be reached fails on the live-page request that follows anyway. Surfacing the error would show a broken resolver instead of masking it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1361},"end":{"line":1370},"content_hash":"703a3db78b676dd197f2df9ff34de6ae420ec599db3f8ddaa20936b9ce708ea8"},"summary":"Surface a failed GET /api/resolve as the tool's error instead of reading the URL as a page","tags":["revisit:every daemon an MCP client may reach serves GET /api/resolve","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T01:47:02.020525Z","id":"5ea0aae90e29b7964920a98a7c8f47d901ef996bdf2d3bd9e70e91865ed7f10e","body":{"detail":"DaemonClient::resolve(id, tid) is already the thread-resolve call (POST …/threads/<tid>/resolve), so the URL resolver is resolve_url.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1443},"end":{"line":1443},"content_hash":"a65b2facec961603c85e2217a66d102352d469480ee47c11f72b40aff90689ea"},"summary":"Name the client's resolver call DaemonClient::resolve","tags":["revisit:the thread call is renamed","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
